{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYG7LY9oAq9E8gkTHuPS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LY818R7dMK7yqDwUVrCZQb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"agent/suggestions.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"## On the scoring rule\"\"\", \"\"\"## On `agent/predict.py`\n\nA1. **`generate()` cannot produce predictions for most of the asset universe.** It builds the\n   context with `MinutePriceStore.load_range`, which raises on a single NaN close. But the model\n   contract states that `context_prices` MAY CONTAIN NaN and that the model must drop rather than\n   interpolate — exactly the situation every com-equ asset (and HYPE) is in. A `--days 7` run\n   aborts with `Local store has 3 missing minute prices in the requested range`, so out of the\n   box the official evaluation only works on BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP. I had to swap that one line for a\n   lenient partition read (reindexed onto a gapless minute grid) to score 14 of the 18\n   asset/configuration combinations. The scoring call is untouched. Worth fixing upstream, since\n   the strict loader is right for realized paths and wrong for contexts.\n\nA2. **`PREDICTIONS_DIR` is a fixed shared path that is never cleared**, and the prediction\n   filenames depend only on `(start, asset, time_length)`. Two `predict.py` runs of *different\n   models* therefore silently overwrite each other's files, and `backtest()` scores whatever is\n   on disk. I lost a 25-minute evaluation to this — a champion and a baseline running\n   concurrently produced plausible-looking but meaningless numbers, with no warning. Either\n   derive the directory from the model identity, or wipe it at the start of a run.\n\n## On the scoring rule\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\n\nj = pathlib.Path(\"agent/journal.md\"); t = j.read_text()\nt += '''\n---\n\n## Iter 9 — Making the official evaluation actually run\n\n**Hypothesis**: the campaign is done; produce the official numbers.\n\n**Change**: ran `agent/predict.py` at 1000 paths over 7 days ending 2026-09-13, for all 18\nasset/configuration combinations, for both the champion and the repo's starting-point model.\n\n**Result**: two infrastructure defects, both of which produced *plausible* output rather than an\nerror, and both worth recording because either one alone would have invalidated the report.\n\n1. **`generate()` aborts on any feed gap.** It builds the context with\n   `MinutePriceStore.load_range`, which raises when a single `close` is NaN. Every com-equ asset\n   and HYPE has gaps, so 14 of the 18 runs died with `Local store has 3 missing minute prices`\n   — and because the driver script piped stdout through `grep \"^summary:\"`, the tracebacks were\n   swallowed and the script reported `DONE` having scored four assets. Fixed by reading the\n   partitions leniently and reindexing onto a gapless minute grid, which is also what makes\n   `[-CONTEXT_MINUTES:]` mean seven *calendar* days. The `backtest()` call is untouched — the\n   metric is still entirely synth-lib's.\n\n2. **Concurrent runs of different models overwrite each other.** `PREDICTIONS_DIR` is a fixed\n   path, never cleared, and filenames are `{start}_{asset}_{time_length}.json` — no model\n   identity. I had launched the champion and the baseline in parallel to save wall-clock; they\n   wrote to the same files and `backtest()` scored whichever landed last. The numbers looked\n   entirely reasonable. Discarded them, gave each model its own directory, reran.\n\n**Verdict**: results below are from the corrected, isolated runs.\n\n**Lesson**: never filter a subprocess's stderr through a grep for the success line. And two\nprocesses that share an output directory are one process.\n'''\nj.write_text(t)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\nsleep 240; cat /workspace/miner_outputs/champ.log; echo ===; cat /workspace/miner_outputs/base.log","description":"Record findings and check progress","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1940,"cache_read_input_tokens":161073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1940,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"cb25789f-907e-48d2-9469-cd70a2d97fd9","timestamp":"2026-09-29T19:12:19.107Z"}
