{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single genuine user message in the entire conversation was: **\"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"**\n\n   `/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md` is the campaign constitution and defines the real intent:\n   - **Objective**: build the price-simulation model with the lowest **CRPS** (lower = better) for Synth Bittensor subnet SN50, handling all three scoring configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP/HYPE, 86400s/300s, 289 pts), COM_EQU_24H (XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX/TSLAX/AAPLX/WTIOIL/SPCX/SP500, 86400s/300s), CRYPTO_1H (crypto, 3600s/60s, 61 pts). 1000 simulations per prompt; honour whatever `num_simulations` is passed.\n   - **Judge every experiment on CRPS**, per configuration and per asset. Field-relative position is explicitly a poor target — \"never trade a CRPS regression for a better one.\"\n   - Champion is evaluated over the **10 days following the 2026-09-14 data cutoff**.\n   - Work solo; no one can answer questions; record decisions in the journal.\n   - **Envelope**: 100.00 USD credits, 18h wall-clock. Read `agent/BUDGET.md` **at the start of each iteration**; a LANDING ORDER there is non-negotiable.\n   - **Nominating is final**: the first time I stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, the campaign is over. **A champion is MANDATORY** — no CHAMPION = Score 0.\n   - **Hardware**: GCP g2-standard-16, 14 CPU / 48GB RAM / 1× NVIDIA L4; only one GPU job at a time.\n\n   **Constraints stated verbatim in CAMPAIGN.md that MUST continue to apply:**\n   1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at `start_time`. Treat everything after **2026-09-14** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 is lookahead into the evaluation window and invalidates the result. Audited on transcript.\n   2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges, aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on transcript.\n   3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester` (via `agent/predict.py`). NEVER reimplement the metric.\n   4. Not allowed: falsifying the journal or results; reproducing another participant's served output as your own. (Studying the field is allowed and recommended; copying an individual miner's served paths is FORBIDDEN.)\n   5. **Keep binary and encoded data out of terminal output.** Read parquet with pandas and `.npy` with numpy — never `cat` a parquet, a git bundle, or model weights; never pipe base64 into context.\n   6. **Start from public sources only**: synth-lib, synth-subnet, the Synth API, and own ideas. The operator's existing miner models must not inform the work; if any turns up, leave it unread and note it in `suggestions.md`.\n   7. Final champion must expose in `agent/modeling.py`: `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` -> `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`, each path `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context. `context_prices` is a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days preceding `start_time` with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`; it MAY CONTAIN NaN — **drop, never interpolate**. Must run OFFLINE.\n   8. **If the model uses randomness, seed it from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`** — read once at the top of `simulate()`, seed every generator; fall back to a chosen seed when absent. Never hardcode a seed that ignores the variable; never leave a generator unseeded.\n   - Other operational rules: always run commands from the workspace root (synth-lib resolves the price store relative to cwd); `market_data/` is READ-ONLY; run everything through `uv run`; do not \"repair\" NaN gaps by interpolating; don't backtest across the three structural breaks (2026-06-23 competition split, 2026-03-11 crypto-1h formula change, ~2026-07-17 SPYX retired / SP500 introduced — **SPYX is DEAD, spend nothing on it**).\n\n   **Required deliverables (in `agent/`, in English, committed to git):** `journal.md` (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson per iteration), `report.md` (explainer style for Synth miners: context, approach, experiments incl. failures, results, limitations, what you'd do with more budget), `CHAMPION` (YAML: `sha` = existing git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles` `[low, high]` if both 24h and 1h supported, `notes` MUST include backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS), `suggestions.md`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **CRPS decomposition**: validator score = **sum of univariate CRPS terms** on *relative price changes over intervals*, in basis points (×10,000). No multivariate term — the joint law of a path matters only through the marginals of aggregated returns.\n   - 24h term budget: 5min 288 terms ≈61%, 30min 48 ≈25%, 3hour 8 ≈10%, 24hour_abs 1 ≈3.6% → ~86% of a 24h score is the marginal distribution of the 5-minute return at each of 288 steps.\n   - crypto-1h: 1/2/5/15/30/60-min intervals, 12 `*_gaps` terms (cumulative return 0→5,10,…,60 min) ≈29%, plus vol CRPS (`vol_60min`, `vol_15min`, `vol_5min`, VOL_CRPS_LAMBDA=5.25) ~1%.\n   - **The central identity (derived this session)**: for a Gaussian forecast of scale σ against truth of scale 1, `E CRPS(σ) = sqrt(2/π)·sqrt(1+σ²) − σ/sqrt(π)`, minimised at σ=1 with value 1/sqrt(π). Expanding: **E CRPS(σ)/E CRPS(1) ≈ 1 + 0.25·(log σ)²**. A 5% scale error costs 0.06%; 20% costs 1%. Therefore a constant scale error is nearly free and **the entire recoverable CRPS is Var(log σ̂ − log σ_true)**. Asymmetry: too wide grows linearly without bound; too narrow saturates at +41% — so the optimum sits slightly below exp(E[log σ]).\n   - **Anchoring**: `context_end(start, time_length) = start − (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS[time_length] + 60)`; ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS = {3600: 60, 86400: 120}. Context ends at start−180s (24h) / start−120s (1h). Relative-change intervals cancel the stale anchor; only ~0.1% extra dispersion on `24hour_abs`. Not worth modelling.\n   - `calculate_total_score_for_miner(simulation_runs, real_price_path, time_increment, scoring_intervals, vol_scoring_blocks)`; `crps_ensemble` from properscoring; `label_observed_blocks` drops NaN; `_abs` intervals divide by `real_price_path[-1] * 10_000`.\n   - Validator prompt start times are **irregular** (~1/h at random minutes); `backtest()` matches within ±30 min (`PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES = 30`); `RealizedPathStore.get` snaps within `PROMPT_START_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES = 30`.\n   - `SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT` is documented but **not set** in this environment; no offline miner_scores bundle exists, so `backtest()` uses the live Synth API for the field.\n   - Time-of-week seasonality; EWMA variance blends at multiple half-lives; log-linear mean reversion of vol; Student-t vs empirical innovations; variance ratios; HAR-style regression; small-sample log-RMS bias.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md`** (read-only) — the constitution; see §1.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/BUDGET.md`** (harness-maintained, read-only). Last read: `Credits: 19.20 / 100.00 USD (19%)`, `Time: 2.7 h elapsed, 15.3 h remaining (15%)`, `Phase: normal`. **Must be re-read at the start of each iteration.**\n   - **`/workspace/DATA.md`** — per-asset coverage; NaN close = no trade; cached realized paths span 2026-06-20 → 2026-09-14.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/modeling.py`** (REWRITTEN this session — the champion entry point). Key content:\n     ```python\n     SCALE_MAP = {\n         \"XAU\": 0.769, \"NVDAX\": 0.758, \"GOOGLX\": 0.744, \"TSLAX\": 0.727,\n         \"AAPLX\": 0.770, \"WTIOIL\": 0.883, \"SPCX\": 0.833, \"SP500\": 0.873,\n     }\n     CHAMPION_SPEC = (\"sv_model\", {\n         \"profile\": \"tow_full.npz\", \"seasonal\": True, \"seas_gamma\": 0.85,\n         \"scale\": 0.90, \"scale_map\": SCALE_MAP, \"dist\": \"t\", \"nu\": 4.0,\n         \"halflives\": (12.0, 72.0, 576.0), \"weights\": (0.3, 0.3, 0.4),\n         \"revert_halflife\": 96.0, \"long_halflife\": 2016.0,\n         \"winsor\": 6.0, \"pool_steps\": 4032,\n     })\n     DEFAULT_SEED = 20260914\n\n     def _seed(asset, start_time) -> int:\n         env = os.environ.get(\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\")\n         base = int(env) if env not in (None, \"\") else DEFAULT_SEED\n         tag = f\"{base}|{asset}|{start_time}\".encode()\n         return int.from_bytes(hashlib.blake2b(tag, digest_size=8).digest(), \"big\") % (2**63 - 1)\n     ```\n     `simulate()` builds `rng = np.random.default_rng(_seed(asset, start_time))`, calls `_model()`, asserts shape `(num_simulations, steps)`, returns `(start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])`. blake2b replaced `hash(str(...))` because Python salts str hashing per process.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/models.py`** — model zoo. Helpers `_step_closes` (unit-independent minute index via `np.asarray(c.index.values, dtype=\"datetime64[m]\").astype(np.int64)`), `_log_returns` (keeps only gap == step_min), `_ewma_sigma`, `_robust_sd`, `_ewma_var_multi`, `_tow_index`. Factories: `baseline_lognormal()`, `iid_model(...)`, `sv_model(...)`, `hvol_model(...)`.\n     `sv_model` signature now includes (added this session): `scale_map=None`, `est: str = \"rms\"`, `level: str = \"ewma\"`, `volfit_art: str = \"volfit_pre0701.npz\"`. Key added code:\n     ```python\n     sc = scale * (1.0 if scale_map is None else float(scale_map.get(asset, 1.0)))\n     sigma_path = np.maximum(sigma_path, MIN_SIGMA) * sc\n     ```\n     and the `level == \"fit\"` branch that recomputes `v0` from the volfit regression using raw (gamma=1) deseasonalised returns.\n     `hvol_model(profile, volfit_art, seas_gamma, scale, dist, nu, vol_of_vol, term=\"fitted\", fallback=None)` builds `V = horizons * np.exp(2.0*yhat)`, log-log interpolates with linear extrapolation below the first knot, differentiates to per-step variance, floors at 5% of the mean. `import volfit as _vf` is now **lazy** (inside the factory).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/volfit.py`** (CREATED this session) — vol-forecast regression, used as a *measurement instrument* only (rejected for the champion). Constants: `HALFLIVES_5 = (12,36,144,576,2016)`, `HALFLIVES_1 = (60,180,720,2880,10080)`, `POOL_5=2016`, `POOL_1=10080`, `WINSOR=6.0`, `HORIZONS_5=(3,12,48,144,288)`, `HORIZONS_1=(2,5,15,30,60)`. Functions: `features(u, halflives)` (log EWMA vols), `build_dataset(asset, step_min, horizons, fit_end, stride_min=60, profile=...)` (multi-horizon targets, y clipped to q02/q98), `log_rms_bias(...)` (non-overlapping-block bias, normalised to 0 at longest horizon), `fit_asset(...)` (ridge, intercept unshrunk, `C[:, 0] -= bias`), `build(fit_end, out_name, profile)`, `load(name)`. `from harness import ...` is now **lazy** inside functions.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/seasonality.py`** — builds `agent/artifacts/tow_pre0701.npz` (fit_end 2026-06-30) and `tow_full.npz`. `BUCKET_MIN=30`, `N_BUCKETS=336`. Winsorised-RMS estimator (clip at 6 robust sigmas, RMS per bucket with ≥20 obs, circular smooth width 5, normalise to mean 1, clip 0.25–4.0). `from harness import ...` now **lazy** inside `fit_profile` and `build`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/calibrate.py`** (CREATED this session):\n     ```python\n     GRID = (0.65, 0.75, 0.85, 0.95, 1.05)\n     def calibrate(factory, kwargs, assets, windows, time_length=86_400, time_increment=300,\n                   cadence_minutes=180, num_simulations=500, grid=GRID, lo=0.55, hi=1.15):\n         # runs each scale, groups by asset, fits a parabola in log-scale, returns argmin clipped\n     ```\n     CLI: `uv run python agent/calibrate.py dev|champ`. `dev` window `[(\"2026-05-20\",\"2026-06-20\")]` with `tow_pre0701.npz`; `champ` `[(\"2026-08-01\",\"2026-09-13\")]` with `tow_full.npz`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/harness.py`** — fast local CRPS harness. `ASSET_COMPETITION_24H` keyed on (asset, time_length); `load_minutes` reads partitions leniently and reindexes to a gapless minute grid; `build_prompts` sets `SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT` around `_fill_gaps_from_realized_paths`; `score_paths` calls `calculate_total_score_for_miner`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/evaluate.py`** / **`/workspace/agent/sweep.py`** — parallel driver + sweep table. `WINDOWS = {\"dev\": [(\"2026-07-05\",\"2026-07-23\")], \"test\": [(\"2026-08-26\",\"2026-09-13\")], \"both\": [...]}`, `ASSETS = {\"crypto\", \"comequ\", \"all24\"}`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/predict.py`** (PATCHED this session) — added `load_context_frame(asset, start, end)` which reads partitions directly and reindexes onto a gapless minute grid, replacing:\n     ```python\n     store = MinutePriceStore(asset, root=store_root(asset))\n     df = store.load_range(start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end).set_index(\"timestamp\")\n     ```\n     with `df = load_context_frame(asset, start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end)`. The `backtest()` scoring call is **untouched**.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent_baseline/`** — `modeling.py` from commit `75b62de` (the starter log-normal martingale) + a copy of the patched `predict.py` with `PREDICTIONS_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign_baseline\" / \"predictions\"`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/official_eval.sh`** (REWRITTEN) — takes `$1` agent dir, `$2` output json, `$3` error log; `emit()` function captures stderr to the ERR log and writes `FAILED <cfg> <asset>` when no summary line appears. Runs 5 crypto-24h + 8 com-equ-24h + 5 crypto-1h at `--days 7 --eval-end 2026-09-13 --num-simulations 1000`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/journal.md`** — Iters 0–9 written. Iter 2 (term budget + oracles), Iter 3 (the scale trap / the identity), Iter 4 (seasonality failure then fix), Iter 5 (vol dynamics dead end), Iter 6 (volfit rejected out of sample, 3 bugs), Iter 7 (per-asset width — the part that generalised), Iter 8 (crypto-1h needs no special model), Iter 9 (making the official evaluation actually run — the two predict.py defects).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/report.md`** (CREATED) — 9 sections. **Section 6 \"Results\" currently contains the placeholder `<!--RESULTS-->` which must be replaced with the official table.**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/suggestions.md`** (CREATED) — items 1–15 plus a new \"On `agent/predict.py`\" section with A1 (strict `load_range` blocks most assets) and A2 (shared `PREDICTIONS_DIR` overwrite hazard).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/diagnose.py`**, **`/workspace/agent/eda_vol.py`** — diagnostics (oracle models, tail stats, variance ratios, persistence).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n\n   - **`hvol_model` scored +1.7–2.5% worse despite a better forecast.** Three distinct causes found and fixed: (a) `np.interp` clamps below its first knot → cumulative variance flat over the first steps → **zero dispersion** at steps 1–2 (fixed with log-log linear extrapolation below the first knot and a 5%-of-mean floor); (b) the fitted term structure was almost entirely **small-sample log bias** (E[log RMS₃] ≈ 45% below log σ for fat tails vs 0.3% at h=288) — fixed by `log_rms_bias()` measured on non-overlapping blocks and subtracted through the intercepts, normalised to 0 at the longest horizon; (c) with `revert_halflife=96` over 288 steps most of the path had already reverted to the EWMA long-run level, so the A/B \"swapping in the regression\" was barely using it.\n   - **`sv_model() got an unexpected keyword argument 'seas_gamma'`** (carried over from before the session) — the edit had not landed; resolved and the sweep re-run successfully.\n   - **Official evaluation silently produced only 4 of 18 results.** `predict.py`'s `generate()` uses `MinutePriceStore.load_range`, which raises `ValueError: Local store has N missing minute prices in the requested range` on any NaN close — so every com-equ asset and HYPE failed. Errors were invisible because the driver piped stdout through `grep \"^summary:\"`. Fixed with the lenient `load_context_frame()` helper and a rewritten driver that logs stderr and emits explicit `FAILED` markers.\n   - **Concurrent champion and baseline runs overwrote each other's predictions.** `PREDICTIONS_DIR` is a fixed shared path, never cleared, and filenames are `{start}_{asset}_{time_length}.json` with no model identity; `backtest()` scores whatever is on disk. The results looked entirely plausible. **All earlier official numbers (including champion BTC 2220.38) were discarded.** Fixed by pointing `agent_baseline/predict.py` at `campaign_baseline/predictions`, wiping both dirs, and relaunching.\n   - **Champion import chain pulled in `harness` (which does `os.chdir()` and imports `synth_lib` at module scope).** `models.py` → `seasonality.py` → `harness.py`, and `models.py` → `volfit.py` → `harness.py`. Fixed by making all `harness` imports lazy (function-level) in `seasonality.py` and `volfit.py`, and making `import volfit` lazy inside `hvol_model`. Verified: importing `modeling` from `/tmp` causes no chdir, loads neither `synth_lib` nor `harness`, and simulates correctly on a NaN-containing context for both 24h and 1h.\n   - **`python` not found** on the PATH — must use `uv run python`.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Solved / concluded:**\n   - Seasonality, after the winsorised-RMS fix, is the single largest win (−1.9%), with γ=0.85 adopted.\n   - Derived and empirically confirmed the CRPS scale identity, which reframed the whole campaign: only `Var(log σ̂ − log σ)` pays. This correctly predicted the oracle gaps and correctly predicted that the MA(1) variance-ratio correction was worth ~0.04% (computed, deliberately not implemented).\n   - Vol-dynamics knobs are saturated: only `revert_halflife=96` matters (−0.56%); everything else <0.1%.\n   - Student-t(4) is worth ~1% over Gaussian; that is the whole prize from distribution shape.\n   - Rejected out of sample: the volfit level (dev −0.09%, test +0.31%), per-asset crypto scales (dev −0.21%, test **+0.13%**), and all crypto-1h-specific tuning (test within ±0.08%).\n   - Kept: com-equ-only scale map with shrink exponent 0.6 (dev −0.21%, **test −0.13%**), justified by parameter stability under refitting four months apart.\n   - One configuration now serves all three competitions. Latency 0.04 s/prompt at 1000 paths (ceiling ~5 s). Seeded reproducibly from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`.\n   - Champion vs the repo's starter model on a spot check (XAU/BTC, 2026-09-05→10): **−10.82%** (BTC −8.43%, XAU −14.26%).\n   - Committed as `a9a8d91`.\n\n   **Ongoing**: the two isolated official evaluation streams (champion and baseline, 18 runs each) were at 11/18 complete with 0 failures at the last poll.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n   - (Plus a continuation instruction to resume from the prior summary without recapping.)\n   - All other inserted blocks were automated `<task-notification>` background-task events explicitly marked NOT user input, system reminders that `agent/BUDGET.md` / `agent/volfit.py` / `agent/suggestions.md` changed on disk, and a git-attribution reminder instructing that commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>` and PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. No other user-role messages exist.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - Wait for the two official evaluation streams to finish (18 runs each), confirm zero `FAILED` entries in `/workspace/miner_outputs/champ.log` and `base.log`.\n   - Build the results table from `/workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ.json` and `off_base.json` (per configuration and per asset, mean CRPS at 1000 paths, champion vs starting point) and replace the `<!--RESULTS-->` placeholder in `agent/report.md` §6.\n   - **Create `agent/CHAMPION`** (YAML: `sha` = an existing git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles: [low, high]`, `notes` containing the backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS). This is MANDATORY — no CHAMPION = Score 0.\n   - Commit everything (journal Iter 9, suggestions A1/A2, report with results, patched `predict.py`, `official_eval.sh`, CHAMPION).\n   - Note in the report/journal the caveat that the shipped `tow_full.npz` and the champion's com-equ map include the backtested windows, so §6 numbers are mildly optimistic relative to the strictly-causal validation numbers in §4–§5.\n   - Re-read `agent/BUDGET.md` at the start of each iteration.\n   - **Remember: nominating is final — the first time I stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, the campaign is over.** So CHAMPION must be written last, after everything else is committed and verified.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   Immediately before this summary request I was polling the two background official-evaluation streams launched after fixing the `PREDICTIONS_DIR` contamination bug. The last poll returned:\n   ```\n   /workspace/miner_outputs/champ.log:11\n   /workspace/miner_outputs/base.log:11\n   ```\n   i.e. 11 of 18 asset/configuration runs complete on each stream, with 0 `FAILED` entries at the prior check. The commands running are:\n   ```\n   bash agent/official_eval.sh agent /workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ.json /workspace/miner_outputs/champ.log\n   bash agent/official_eval.sh agent_baseline /workspace/miner_outputs/off_base.json /workspace/miner_outputs/base.log\n   ```\n   Each `emit` line appends a JSON record of the form `{\"cfg\":\"<cfg>\",\"asset\":\"<A>\",\"s\":{...summary...}}` to the output file. Budget at the last read: 19.20/100 USD, 2.7 h elapsed, 15.3 h remaining.\n\n   Just before polling, I had verified the sweep pipeline still works after the lazy-import refactor, producing the headline comparison against the repo's starter model:\n   ```\n   asset    BTC_%  XAU_%  MEAN_%\n   champ    -8.43 -14.26  -10.82\n   starter   0.00   0.00    0.00\n   ```\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Continue polling until both streams report 18 `ok` lines and `DONE`, then parse `off_champ.json` / `off_base.json` into the per-configuration results table, fill the `<!--RESULTS-->` placeholder in `agent/report.md`, write `agent/CHAMPION`, and commit.\n\n   This directly continues the task I was on: I had just written in `agent/report.md` §6 \"Backtested with `agent/predict.py` (the official `synth_lib.backtester`), 7 days of prompts ending 2026-09-13, 1000 simulated paths — the same count the validator serves.\" followed by the literal placeholder `<!--RESULTS-->`, and in journal Iter 9: \"**Verdict**: results below are from the corrected, isolated runs.\" — both of which require the numbers now being produced.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"c172c2d9-9572-4aec-bfcb-cdc4e9e486c2","timestamp":"2026-09-29T19:58:04.832Z","isSynthetic":true}
