{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single genuine user message in the entire conversation was: **\"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"** (plus a continuation instruction to resume from the prior summary without recapping).\n\n   `/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md` is the campaign constitution and defines the real intent:\n   - **Objective**: build the price-simulation model with the lowest **CRPS** (lower = better) for Synth Bittensor subnet SN50, handling all three scoring configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP/HYPE, 86400s/300s, 289 pts), COM_EQU_24H (XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX/TSLAX/AAPLX/WTIOIL/SPCX/SP500, 86400s/300s), CRYPTO_1H (crypto, 3600s/60s, 61 pts). 1000 simulations per prompt; honour whatever `num_simulations` is passed.\n   - **Judge every experiment on CRPS**, per configuration and per asset. Field-relative position is explicitly a poor target — \"never trade a CRPS regression for a better one.\"\n   - Champion is evaluated over the **10 days following the 2026-09-14 data cutoff**.\n   - Work solo; no one can answer questions; record decisions in the journal.\n   - **Envelope**: 100.00 USD credits, 18h wall-clock. Read `agent/BUDGET.md` **at the start of each iteration**; a LANDING ORDER there is non-negotiable.\n   - **Nominating is final**: the first time I stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, the campaign is over. **A champion is MANDATORY** — no CHAMPION = Score 0.\n   - **Hardware**: GCP g2-standard-16, 14 CPU / 48GB RAM / 1× NVIDIA L4; only one GPU job at a time.\n\n   **Constraints stated verbatim in CAMPAIGN.md that MUST continue to apply:**\n   1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at `start_time`. Treat everything after **2026-09-14** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 is lookahead into the evaluation window and invalidates the result. Audited on transcript.\n   2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges, aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on transcript.\n   3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester` (via `agent/predict.py`). NEVER reimplement the metric.\n   4. Not allowed: falsifying the journal or results; reproducing another participant's served output as your own. (Studying the field is allowed and recommended; copying an individual miner's served paths is FORBIDDEN.)\n   5. **Keep binary and encoded data out of terminal output.** Read parquet with pandas and `.npy` with numpy — never `cat` a parquet, a git bundle, or model weights; never pipe base64 into context.\n   6. **Start from public sources only**: synth-lib, synth-subnet, the Synth API, and own ideas. The operator's existing miner models must not inform the work; if any turns up, leave it unread and note it in `suggestions.md`.\n   7. Final champion must expose in `agent/modeling.py`: `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` -> `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`, each path `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context. `context_prices` is a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days preceding `start_time` with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`; it MAY CONTAIN NaN — **drop, never interpolate**. Must run OFFLINE.\n   8. **If the model uses randomness, seed it from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`** — read once at the top of `simulate()`, seed every generator; fall back to a chosen seed when absent. Never hardcode a seed that ignores the variable; never leave a generator unseeded.\n   - Other operational rules: always run commands from the workspace root (synth-lib resolves the price store relative to cwd); `market_data/` is READ-ONLY; run everything through `uv run`; do not \"repair\" NaN gaps by interpolating; don't backtest across the three structural breaks (2026-06-23 competition split, 2026-03-11 crypto-1h formula change, ~2026-07-17 SPYX retired / SP500 introduced — **SPYX is DEAD, spend nothing on it**).\n\n   **Required deliverables (in `agent/`, in English, committed to git):** `journal.md` (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson per iteration), `report.md` (explainer style for Synth miners), `CHAMPION` (YAML: `sha` = existing git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles` `[low, high]`, `notes` MUST include backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS), `suggestions.md`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **CRPS decomposition**: validator score = **sum of univariate CRPS terms** on *relative price changes over intervals*, in basis points. No multivariate term. 24h term budget: 5min 288 terms ≈61%, 30min 48 ≈25%, 3hour 8 ≈10%, 24hour_abs 1 ≈3.6%.\n   - **The central identity**: `E CRPS(σ) = sqrt(2/π)·sqrt(1+σ²) − σ/sqrt(π)`, minimised at σ=1. Expanding: **E CRPS(σ)/E CRPS(1) ≈ 1 + 0.25·(log σ)²**. A constant scale error is nearly free; **the entire recoverable CRPS is Var(log σ̂ − log σ_true)**. Asymmetry: too wide grows linearly; too narrow saturates at +41%.\n   - **NEW — the level confound (Iter 12)**: the profile is mean-normalised to 1, so by Jensen `E[s^γ]` *grows* with γ. A 1-D sweep of a shape parameter at fixed scale measures the *level*, which §2 says is nearly free. **Sweep shape parameters with the level re-optimised at every point.**\n   - **The transfer criterion**: parameter stability under refitting four months apart predicts out-of-sample transfer better than in-sample gain. Effects under ~0.1%, or that disagree in sign between windows, are noise.\n   - Backtester `en_ = max(start_time) + 26h` and day-granular partition walking — the snapshot edge is the last timestamp minus whatever lookahead the *scoring* code adds.\n   - Time-of-week seasonality; EWMA variance blends at multiple half-lives; log-linear mean reversion of vol; Student-t(4) innovations; Parkinson/Garman-Klass range estimators; small-sample log-RMS bias.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/BUDGET.md`** (harness-maintained, read-only). Last read: `Credits: 33.14 / 100.00 USD (33%)`, `Time: 5.0 h elapsed, 13.0 h remaining (28%)`, `Phase: normal`. **Must be re-read at the start of each iteration.**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/modeling.py`** (champion entry point, UPDATED this segment):\n     ```python\n     SCALE_MAP = {\n         \"XAU\": 0.725, \"NVDAX\": 0.721, \"GOOGLX\": 0.713, \"TSLAX\": 0.678,\n         \"AAPLX\": 0.758, \"WTIOIL\": 0.906, \"SPCX\": 0.847, \"SP500\": 0.889,\n     }\n     # Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. ...\n     SEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n     CHAMPION_SPEC = (\"sv_model\", {\n         \"profile\": \"tow_full.npz\", \"seasonal\": True, \"seas_gamma\": SEAS_GAMMA,\n         \"scale\": 0.90, \"scale_map\": SCALE_MAP, \"dist\": \"t\", \"nu\": 4.0,\n         \"halflives\": (12.0, 72.0, 576.0), \"weights\": (0.3, 0.3, 0.4),\n         \"revert_halflife\": 96.0, \"long_halflife\": 2016.0,\n         \"winsor\": 6.0, \"pool_steps\": 4032,\n     })\n     DEFAULT_SEED = 20260914\n     def _seed(asset, start_time) -> int:   # blake2b(f\"{base}|{asset}|{start_time}\")\n     ```\n     Verified from `/tmp`: no chdir, no `synth_lib`/`harness` import, correct shapes for both horizons on a NaN-containing context, seed-reproducible across reloads, 0.04 s/prompt (24h) and 0.01 s/prompt (1h) at 1000 paths.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/models.py`** (model zoo, MODIFIED). `sv_model` signature now includes:\n     ```python\n     seas_gamma: float | dict = 1.0,\n     seas_gamma_lo: float | dict | None = None,   # rejected experiment, default is a no-op\n     act_beta: float = 0.0,\n     act_halflives=(24.0, 1152.0),\n     act_cap: float = 1.30,\n     ```\n     New factory-level code replacing the old single-γ transform:\n     ```python\n     _gammas = dict(seas_gamma) if isinstance(seas_gamma, dict) else None\n     _gammas_lo = dict(seas_gamma_lo) if isinstance(seas_gamma_lo, dict) else None\n     _prof_cache: dict[tuple, dict] = {}\n\n     def _bend(v, g_hi, g_lo):\n         out = np.where(v >= 1.0, v**g_hi, v**g_lo)\n         return out / out.mean()\n\n     def _profile_for(step_min: int):\n         g = float(_gammas.get(step_min, 1.0)) if _gammas is not None else float(seas_gamma)\n         if seas_gamma_lo is None:\n             g_lo = g\n         else:\n             g_lo = (float(_gammas_lo.get(step_min, 1.0)) if _gammas_lo is not None\n                     else float(seas_gamma_lo))\n         key = (g, g_lo)\n         if key not in _prof_cache:\n             _prof_cache[key] = (prof_raw if g == 1.0 and g_lo == 1.0\n                                 else {k: _bend(v, g, g_lo) for k, v in prof_raw.items()})\n         return _prof_cache[key]\n     ```\n     Inside `f`: `p = _profile_for(step_min).get(key)`. And at the scaling step:\n     ```python\n     sc = scale * (1.0 if scale_map is None else float(scale_map.get(asset, 1.0)))\n     if act_beta:\n         sc *= _activity_mult(context_prices, step_min, asset, prof_raw,\n                              act_beta, act_halflives, act_cap)\n     sigma_path = np.maximum(sigma_path, MIN_SIGMA) * sc\n     ```\n     New module-level helper `_activity_mult(context_prices, step_min, asset, prof_raw, beta, halflives, cap)` — resamples `trade_count` to step bars, divides by the `{asset}_act` profile, takes `log EWMA(fast) − log EWMA(slow)` of `log1p`, returns `clip(exp(beta*a), 1/cap, cap)`, and returns `1.0` if the column is missing or `< 200` finite bars.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/seasonality.py`** (EXTENDED). Added `fit_activity(asset, fit_end=None, smooth=5)` — geometric-mean (`log1p`/`expm1`) time-of-week profile of `trade_count`, circularly smoothed, normalised to mean 1, clipped 0.02–20.0. `build()` now also writes `data[f\"{asset}_act\"]`. Both artifacts rebuilt: `tow_pre0701.npz` and `tow_full.npz`, 39 profiles each. The volatility profiles are unchanged (deterministic `fit_profile`).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/official_eval.sh`** (24h legs only now): `END=2026-09-13; DAYS=7; N=1000`; 5 crypto-24h + 8 com-equ-24h; the crypto-1h loop replaced by a comment pointing at `official_eval_1h.sh`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/official_eval_1h.sh`** (CREATED): identical `emit()` but `END=2026-09-12`, does not truncate `$OUT`/`$ERR`, runs the 5 crypto-1h assets with `--time-increment 60 --time-length 3600`, writes `DONE-1H $DIR`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/results_table.py`** (CREATED): reads `miner_outputs/off_champ.json` and `off_base.json` (one JSON record per line, `{\"cfg\":..,\"asset\":..,\"s\":{summary}}`), renders three markdown tables with per-asset and mean rows plus % change. Used to patch report §6.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/eda_range.py`** (CREATED, negative result): aggregates 1-min bars to 5-min high/low/close, builds close²/Parkinson/Garman-Klass variance proxies, deseasonalises, runs each through the champion's EWMA blend, compares **centred** log-error sd vs realized 288-step vol. Output: `d_park_% -0.161`, `d_gk_% -0.272`, `d_mix_% -0.073` (negative = worse).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/eda_activity.py`** (CREATED): incremental out-of-sample regression (60/40 time split) of log realized future vol on the champion's own vol predictor alone vs. plus activity features (fast−slow log EWMA of deseasonalised `trade_count` and `volume`, plus the slow count level). Output: BTC −0.067, ETH +0.002, SOL +0.015, XRP +0.159, HYPE +0.031, XAU +9.185 (untrustworthy, sd_base 3.08), NVDAX +0.237, GOOGLX +0.285, TSLAX +0.505, AAPLX +0.011, WTIOIL −2.681, SPCX −0.534, SP500 +0.066; mean +0.555.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/gamma_fit.py`** (CREATED): per-asset γ fit via parabola on `GRID = (0.55, 0.70, 0.85, 1.00, 1.15)`. `FITS` dict documents `fitA` as **wrong by construction** (window inside the profile's own fit span) alongside the two causal windows `fitD`/`fitT`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/journal.md`** — Iters 0–13. Iter 10 (the snapshot edge + disclosure of the synth-lib-internal 09-15 price request), Iter 11 (range estimators rejected), Iter 12 (the seasonal exponent was confounded with the level — the costliest mistake), Iter 13 (re-audit of every other knob with the level free).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/report.md`** — §3 model description updated (γ 1.35/0.85, com-equ multipliers 0.61–0.91); §4 seasonality headline now \"−1.9 %, plus −0.5 % from the exponent\"; §5 gained two new subsections (\"The seasonal exponent was confounded with the level\", \"Range-based volatility estimators\"); §6 tables filled with the final official numbers and a note that the 24h legs end 2026-09-13 and the 1h leg 2026-09-12; §8 item 1 rewritten around the interface constraint, item 4 rewritten, item 5 added; §9 repro block updated with both eval scripts and `results_table.py`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/suggestions.md`** — items 1–15 plus A1 (strict `load_range` blocks most assets), A2 (shared `PREDICTIONS_DIR` overwrite hazard), and **new A3** (the 26h buffer + ingest into a read-only mount; the buffer should be `time_length + tolerance`, and the ingest should be gated by the offline flag).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent_baseline/`** — starter model from `75b62de` plus a copy of the patched `predict.py` pointed at `miner_outputs/campaign_baseline/predictions`.\n\n   - Git commits this segment: `3ee0d02` (official evaluation, all 18), `6cded26` (step-keyed seasonal exponent), `03f5877` (official re-evaluation + Iter 13).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n\n   - **All 10 crypto-1h official runs failed** with `OSError: [Errno 30] Read-only file system: 'market_data/prices/<A>/1m/date=2026-09-15.parquet'`. Cause: `backtest()` step 5 requests prices to `max(start_time) + 26h`; `download_price_data` walks whole-day partitions and sends absent days to `MinutePriceStore.ingest_range`, which fetches then tries to persist. 24h prompts are scorable only 24h later so they stop at 09-12 (+26h inside the snapshot); 1h prompts reach 09-13 22:00 (+26h = 09-15). Fixed by moving the 1h leg to `--eval-end 2026-09-12` in a separate script. Disclosed in journal Iter 10: synth-lib itself issued a post-cutoff price request, every run raised and produced no output, and no result/parameter/decision derives from it.\n   - **γ fitted on 2026-05-20..06-20 sent all 13 assets to the top of the grid.** That window lies inside the span `tow_pre0701.npz` was fitted on, so the profile was in-sample there. Discarded; refit on windows where the profile is strictly causal.\n   - **The shipped `seas_gamma = 0.85` was wrong.** The original 1-D sweep held `scale` fixed and was reading the width *level*, not the profile shape. With scale re-optimised at each γ, the optimum is interior near 1.35 for 5-min steps. Fixed by making `seas_gamma` a dict keyed on step size and refitting the com-equ scale map at the new γ.\n   - (Carried from earlier, already fixed): `predict.py`'s strict `MinutePriceStore.load_range` blocking every NaN-bearing asset; concurrent runs overwriting a shared `PREDICTIONS_DIR`; `python` not on PATH (must use `uv run`).\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Completed and verified:**\n   - All 18 asset/configuration official runs completed for both champion and starting point, zero failures.\n   - Final official results (7 days of prompts, 1000 paths, via `agent/predict.py`): **CRYPTO_24H mean 3527.7 vs 3680.1 (−4.14%)**; **COM_EQU_24H mean 1824.9 vs 2076.5 (−12.11%)**; **CRYPTO_1H mean 799.5 vs 831.9 (−3.90%)**. Champion ahead on **all 18**.\n   - The γ change improved 12 of 13 24h assets officially (NVDAX +0.33% the only regression); crypto-1h returned **bit-identical** numbers, confirming the step-keyed exponent touched only the 5-minute step.\n   - Validated on a third window (2026-07-24..08-25) untouched by every earlier experiment.\n   - Cross-asset pooling established as **precluded by the interface** — `simulate()` receives one asset's context only.\n\n   **Rejected on evidence this segment:** Parkinson/Garman-Klass range estimators (worse); per-asset γ fitted on a profile-in-sample window (artefact); asymmetric γ (`seas_gamma_lo`) — dev and test disagree on sign; `halflives=(12,144,1152)` (−0.05/−0.03%, below the transfer threshold); everything in the Iter 13 re-audit.\n\n   **Just concluded (result in hand, not yet written up):** the bounded activity multiplier. `/tmp/act.py` swept `act_beta ∈ {+0.10, +0.20, +0.35, +0.55, −0.20}` with scale re-optimised over {0.85, 0.90, 0.95}, separately for comequ and crypto, on dev and test. **Every non-zero β is worse on both windows for both groups** — comequ: +0.236%/+0.105% at β=+0.10 rising monotonically to +1.040%/+0.616% at β=+0.55, and β=−0.20 also worse (+0.111%/+0.390%); crypto: +0.126%/+0.048% at β=+0.10 up to +0.930%/+0.696% at β=+0.55. So `act_beta = 0` (the current champion) wins — the incremental regression signal in `eda_activity.py` does not convert into CRPS.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n   - A continuation instruction to resume from the prior summary without recapping or prefacing.\n   - The final message instructing that this summary be produced as text only, with no tool calls.\n   - All other inserted blocks were automated `<task-notification>` background-task events explicitly marked NOT user input, system reminders that files changed on disk (`agent/BUDGET.md`, `agent/official_eval.sh`, `agent/report.md`, `agent/suggestions.md`, `agent/volfit.py`), and a git-attribution reminder instructing that commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>` and PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. No other user-role messages exist.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - Write up the activity-multiplier negative result as journal Iter 14 and add a short entry to `agent/report.md` §5 (and reconcile §8 item 3, which still proposes using `volume`/`trade_count`, with the finding that the signal does not convert to CRPS).\n   - Decide whether to leave `act_beta`/`_activity_mult`/`seas_gamma_lo`/`fit_activity` in the codebase (all are no-ops at their defaults) or strip them; note that `tow_*.npz` now carry the extra `{asset}_act` arrays.\n   - Commit the `seas_gamma_lo`, `_activity_mult`, `fit_activity`, `eda_activity.py` and rebuilt-artifact changes (currently uncommitted).\n   - Re-read `agent/BUDGET.md` at the start of each iteration; honour any LANDING ORDER immediately.\n   - **Create `agent/CHAMPION` LAST** (YAML: `sha` = an existing git commit — currently `03f5877` or later, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles: [low, high]`, `notes` containing the backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS). This is MANDATORY — no CHAMPION = Score 0 — but **nominating is final**, so it must be written only after everything else is committed and verified.\n   - Keep the report's existing caveat that `tow_full.npz` and the com-equ map include the backtested windows, so §6 numbers are mildly optimistic relative to the strictly-causal §4–§5 validation numbers.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   Immediately before this summary request I had just received the output of the activity-multiplier CRPS sweep — the final experiment in the line that began with `agent/eda_activity.py`. Having found real incremental regression signal on the tokenised equities but two blowups, I had said: *\"That argues for one bounded parameter, not a regression\"*, added `fit_activity()` to `agent/seasonality.py`, rebuilt both artifacts (39 profiles each), added `_activity_mult()` plus `act_beta`/`act_halflives`/`act_cap` to `agent/models.py`, and run `/tmp/act.py`. The returned table shows β=0 (the unchanged champion) best on both dev and test for both comequ and crypto, with the penalty growing monotonically in |β|. Nothing had yet been written to the journal or report about it, and none of the supporting code changes had been committed.\n\n   The champion model itself is unchanged by this experiment and stands at commit `03f5877` with `SEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}` and the refit `SCALE_MAP`. Budget at last read: 33.14/100 USD, 5.0 h elapsed, 13.0 h remaining, phase normal.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Write journal Iter 14 recording the activity-multiplier rejection (signal exists in an incremental log-vol regression — TSLAX +0.50%, GOOGLX +0.28%, NVDAX +0.24% — but a bounded single-coefficient version is worse on both windows at every β tested, and the regression's own WTIOIL −2.68% / SPCX −0.53% blowups explain why), add the corresponding short subsection to `agent/report.md` §5, reconcile §8 item 3, and commit the uncommitted `models.py` / `seasonality.py` / `eda_activity.py` / artifact changes.\n\n   This directly continues the experiment I was on. Verbatim from my last message before the result arrived: *\"Real incremental signal on the tokenised equities (TSLAX +0.50%, GOOGLX +0.28%, NVDAX +0.24%), nothing on crypto, and two blowups (WTIOIL −2.68%) that say a free linear fit is fragile. That argues for one bounded parameter, not a regression.\"* — and the sweep has now answered that the bounded parameter does not pay either.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface