{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJws5TV6bWkJbDdEMm3Yp9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. The two horizons want\n# opposite corrections and three disjoint windows agree on both signs: at the 5-minute step the\n# profile must be *amplified* (the winsorised-RMS estimator, the circular smoothing and the\n# 0.25-4.0 clip all shrink it toward flat, and 1.35 un-shrinks it), while at the 1-minute step\n# 30-minute buckets are coarse relative to the step and amplifying them only adds noise.\nSEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n\n=== report:\n### Time-of-week seasonality (−1.9 %, plus −0.5 % from the exponent) — the largest single win\n\nVolatility in these markets is strongly deterministic in time-of-week, and a constant σ is\nsimultaneously too wide overnight and too narrow at the US cash open. CRPS charges for both.\nThis is worth −1.9 % across 13 assets, concentrated in com-equ (NVDAX −3.5 %, TSLAX −3.8 %,\nGOOGLX −3.2 %). A further −0.5 % came from the *exponent* on the profile, which I had wrong for\nmost of the campaign — see \"The seasonal exponent was confounded with the level\" in §5.\n\n### Student-t(4) innovations (−1 %)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"66a626a8-d36c-4fc4-b994-4333afa80e9a","timestamp":"2026-09-29T22:52:11.626Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. The two horizons want\n# opposite corrections and three disjoint windows agree on both signs: at the 5-minute step the\n# profile must be *amplified* (the winsorised-RMS estimator, the circular smoothing and the\n# 0.25-4.0 clip all shrink it toward flat, and 1.35 un-shrinks it), while at the 1-minute step\n# 30-minute buckets are coarse relative to the step and amplifying them only adds noise.\nSEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n\n=== report:\n### Time-of-week seasonality (−1.9 %, plus −0.5 % from the exponent) — the largest single win\n\nVolatility in these markets is strongly deterministic in time-of-week, and a constant σ is\nsimultaneously too wide overnight and too narrow at the US cash open. CRPS charges for both.\nThis is worth −1.9 % across 13 assets, concentrated in com-equ (NVDAX −3.5 %, TSLAX −3.8 %,\nGOOGLX −3.2 %). A further −0.5 % came from the *exponent* on the profile, which I had wrong for\nmost of the campaign — see \"The seasonal exponent was confounded with the level\" in §5.\n\n### Student-t(4) innovations (−1 %)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYYuLR7L5CJb7PHS5GcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kwBo8tXVaUSpoepejbf2g","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"agent/modeling.py\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"# 30-minute buckets are coarse relative to the step and amplifying them only adds noise.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"# it must be *damped*. The damping is a property of the return, not of the profile: a 1-minute\n# print carries bid-ask bounce and zero-return minutes, width that does not follow time-of-week,\n# so the seasonal share of it is genuinely smaller. Refining the profile to 10-minute buckets\n# leaves the 1-minute step unchanged to three decimals (journal Iter 15).\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nsed -n '58,66p' agent/modeling.py","description":"Correct the gamma explanation in modeling.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":88658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":602,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"2e2cb491-5f55-4e79-b4f2-085b3e390919","timestamp":"2026-09-29T22:52:15.964Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014kwBo8tXVaUSpoepejbf2g","type":"tool_result","content":"# Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. The two horizons want\n# opposite corrections and three disjoint windows agree on both signs: at the 5-minute step the\n# profile must be *amplified* (the winsorised-RMS estimator, the circular smoothing and the\n# 0.25-4.0 clip all shrink it toward flat, and 1.35 un-shrinks it), while at the 1-minute step\n# it must be *damped*. The damping is a property of the return, not of the profile: a 1-minute\n# print carries bid-ask bounce and zero-return minutes, width that does not follow time-of-week,\n# so the seasonal share of it is genuinely smaller. Refining the profile to 10-minute buckets\n# leaves the 1-minute step unchanged to three decimals (journal Iter 15).\nSEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"87312b84-399a-4305-aece-26ef336614d3","timestamp":"2026-09-29T22:52:16.094Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. The two horizons want\n# opposite corrections and three disjoint windows agree on both signs: at the 5-minute step the\n# profile must be *amplified* (the winsorised-RMS estimator, the circular smoothing and the\n# 0.25-4.0 clip all shrink it toward flat, and 1.35 un-shrinks it), while at the 1-minute step\n# it must be *damped*. The damping is a property of the return, not of the profile: a 1-minute\n# print carries bid-ask bounce and zero-return minutes, width that does not follow time-of-week,\n# so the seasonal share of it is genuinely smaller. Refining the profile to 10-minute buckets\n# leaves the 1-minute step unchanged to three decimals (journal Iter 15).\nSEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"fil