{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRe3nT1sT7TW1W9581jykE","type":"tool_result","content":"### Volatility mean reversion (−0.6 %)\n\nReverting the current EWMA level toward the 7-day level with a 96-step half-life. This was the\n*only* one of the vol-dynamics knobs that mattered — see §5.\n\n### A per-asset width multiplier for com-equ (−0.13 % out of sample)\n\nFitted on a window preceding both validation windows. Small, but it is the part of the per-asset\ncalibration that demonstrably generalises, and the diagnosis is the interesting bit (§5).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"c34d2cb4-3844-452d-94e8-b062ff05f4f0","timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:35:29.004Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Volatility mean reversion (−0.6 %)\n\nReverting the current EWMA level toward the 7-day level with a 96-step half-life. This was the\n*only* one of the vol-dynamics knobs that mattered — see §5.\n\n### A per-asset width multiplier for com-equ (−0.13 % out of sample)\n\nFitted on a window preceding both validation windows. Small, but it is the part of the per-asset\ncalibration that demonstrably generalises, and the diagnosis is the interesting bit (§5).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYcCoZ4vhM2YRvQykAu2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CFfDP17LrYwwoBMxCEVA2Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"agent/report.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"### A per-asset width multiplier for com-equ (−0.13 % out of sample)\n\nFitted on a window preceding both validation windows. Small, but it is the part of the per-asset\ncalibration that demonstrably generalises, and the diagnosis is the interesting bit (§5).\"\"\"\nnew = old + \"\"\"\n\n### Fattening the aggregated intervals (−0.10 % on com-equ, three windows)\n\nThe last thing I found, and the only one that came from reading the score's *shape* rather than\nits level. About 39 % of a 24-hour score is charged on intervals longer than one step — 30-min,\n3-hour, 24-hour — and ~29 % of a 1-hour score on the cumulative `*_gaps` terms. With a σ path\nthat is deterministic given the context, those aggregates are sums of independent innovations,\nso the CLT makes them close to Gaussian; real ones are not, because volatility clusters *inside*\nthe window.\n\nA persistent AR(1) factor in log-volatility fixes that, but only if it is renormalised so every\nstep's variance is exactly unchanged — otherwise it also perturbs the 61 % of the score that was\nalready calibrated, which is why the constant-per-path version of the same idea (`vol_of_vol`,\nthe half-life→∞ limit) had failed earlier. With the constraint it is worth −0.096 %, −0.096 %,\n−0.102 % on three disjoint com-equ windows. On crypto it changes sign between windows and is\nleft off.\n\nIt comes with a level correction that §2 predicts: a fatter mixture at fixed variance is\n*narrower in the bulk*, so the CRPS-optimal width moves up — 0.90 → 0.95, on all three windows.\nShip the shape change without the level change and you give most of it back.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\nsleep 200; grep -c . /workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ2.json; tail -2 /tmp/off2.log","description":"Add section 4 subsection, check eval progress","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":346,"cache_read_input_tokens":138705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":346,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"f9b60d96-595e-41c7-ae54-653e46478f85","timestamp":"2026-09-29T23:35:38.325Z"}
