{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single genuine user message in the entire conversation was: **\"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"** (plus a continuation instruction to resume from a prior summary without recapping, and the final instruction to produce this summary as text only).\n\n   `/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md` is the campaign constitution:\n   - **Objective**: build the price-simulation model with the lowest **CRPS** (lower = better) for Synth Bittensor subnet SN50, across three scoring configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP/HYPE, 86400s/300s, 289 pts), COM_EQU_24H (XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX/TSLAX/AAPLX/WTIOIL/SPCX/SP500, 86400s/300s), CRYPTO_1H (crypto, 3600s/60s, 61 pts). 1000 simulations per prompt; honour whatever `num_simulations` is passed.\n   - **Judge every experiment on CRPS**, per configuration and per asset. Field-relative position is a poor target — \"never trade a CRPS regression for a better one.\"\n   - Champion is evaluated over the **10 days following the 2026-09-14 data cutoff**.\n   - Work solo; no one can answer questions; record decisions in the journal.\n   - **Envelope**: 100.00 USD credits, 18h wall-clock. Read `agent/BUDGET.md` **at the start of each iteration**; a LANDING ORDER there is non-negotiable.\n   - **Nominating is final**: the first time I stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, the campaign is over. **A champion is MANDATORY** — no CHAMPION = Score 0.\n   - **Hardware**: GCP g2-standard-16, 14 CPU / 48GB RAM / 1× NVIDIA L4; only one GPU job at a time.\n\n   **Constraints stated verbatim in CAMPAIGN.md that MUST continue to apply:**\n   1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at `start_time`. Treat everything after **2026-09-14** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 is lookahead into the evaluation window and invalidates the result. Audited on transcript.\n   2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges, aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on transcript.\n   3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester` (via `agent/predict.py`). NEVER reimplement the metric.\n   4. Not allowed: falsifying the journal or results; reproducing another participant's served output as your own. (Studying the field is allowed; copying an individual miner's served paths is FORBIDDEN.)\n   5. **Keep binary and encoded data out of terminal output.** Read parquet with pandas and `.npy` with numpy — never `cat` a parquet, a git bundle, or model weights; never pipe base64 into context.\n   6. **Start from public sources only**: synth-lib, synth-subnet, the Synth API, and own ideas. The operator's existing miner models must not inform the work; if any turns up, leave it unread and note it in `suggestions.md`.\n   7. Final champion must expose in `agent/modeling.py`: `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` -> `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`, each path `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context. `context_prices` is a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days preceding `start_time` with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`; it MAY CONTAIN NaN — **drop, never interpolate**. Must run OFFLINE.\n   8. **If the model uses randomness, seed it from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`** — read once at the top of `simulate()`, seed every generator; fall back to a chosen seed when absent. Never hardcode a seed that ignores the variable; never leave a generator unseeded.\n   - Other operational rules: always run commands from the workspace root (synth-lib resolves the price store relative to cwd); `market_data/` is READ-ONLY; run everything through `uv run`; don't backtest across the three structural breaks (2026-06-23 competition split, 2026-03-11 crypto-1h formula change, ~2026-07-17 SPYX retired / SP500 introduced — **SPYX is DEAD, spend nothing on it**).\n\n   **Required deliverables (in `agent/`, in English, committed to git):** `journal.md` (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson per iteration), `report.md` (explainer style for Synth miners), `CHAMPION` (YAML: `sha` = existing git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles` `[low, high]`, `notes` MUST include backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS), `suggestions.md`.\n\n   **Mid-conversation system instruction (still in effect):** while bypass permissions mode is active, do work through the Bash tool wherever it can accomplish the job (cat/sed/grep/heredocs/short scripts) rather than the dedicated Read/Edit/Write tools; fall back to a dedicated tool only when Bash genuinely cannot do the job.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **CRPS decomposition**: validator score = **sum of univariate CRPS terms** on *relative price changes over intervals*, in basis points. No multivariate term. 24h term budget: 5min 288 terms ≈61%, 30min 48 ≈25%, 3hour 8 ≈10%, 24hour_abs 1 ≈3.6%. CRYPTO_1H: 1/2/5/15/30/60-minute intervals plus twelve `*_gaps` terms (cumulative return from start) worth ≈29%, plus a ~1% volatility-CRPS block.\n   - **The central identity**: `E CRPS(σ) = sqrt(2/π)·sqrt(1+σ²) − σ/sqrt(π)`, minimised at σ=1. Expanding: **E CRPS(σ)/E CRPS(1) ≈ 1 + 0.25·(log σ)²**. A constant scale error is nearly free; **the entire recoverable CRPS is Var(log σ̂ − log σ_true)**. Asymmetry: too wide grows linearly; too narrow saturates at +41%, so the CRPS-optimal width sits slightly *below* `exp(E[log σ])`.\n   - **The oracle gap**: an oracle handed the realized vol of the window it predicts scores ≈6% better than the causal champion on crypto-24h. That bounds the level-forecasting pot.\n   - **The level confound (Iter 12)**: the profile is mean-normalised to 1, so by Jensen `E[s^γ]` grows with γ. **Sweep shape parameters with the level re-optimised at every point.**\n   - **The transfer criterion**: parameter stability under refitting predicts out-of-sample transfer better than in-sample gain. Effects under ~0.1%, or that disagree in sign between windows, are noise.\n   - **NEW — the redundancy principle (Iter 16)**: range estimators, trade activity and leverage all failed because each acts on future volatility *through* realized volatility, which a fast EWMA already prices in. Only forward-looking (scheduled) information can be incremental — which is why the time-of-week profile is the largest win.\n   - **NEW — shape vs level (Iter 17)**: ~39% of a 24h score is on aggregated intervals; a deterministic σ path makes those too Gaussian by the CLT. A persistent AR(1) factor in log-vol renormalised to preserve each step's variance exactly fattens the aggregates without disturbing the already-calibrated 61%.\n   - Three validation windows: **dev** 2026-07-05..07-23, **val3** 2026-07-24..08-25, **test** 2026-08-26..09-13.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/BUDGET.md`** (harness-maintained, read-only). Last read: `Credits: 50.34 / 100.00 USD (50%)`, `Time: 7.2 h elapsed, 10.8 h remaining (40%)`, `Phase: normal`. **Must be re-read at the start of each iteration.**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/modeling.py`** (champion entry point, MODIFIED this segment). Current state:\n     ```python\n     _LEV = 0.95 / 0.90\n     # Global width level, keyed by step size in minutes. ...\n     SCALE = {5: 0.90, 1: 0.95}\n     SCALE_MAP = {\"XAU\": 0.725*_LEV, \"NVDAX\": 0.721*_LEV, \"GOOGLX\": 0.713*_LEV,\n                  \"TSLAX\": 0.678*_LEV, \"AAPLX\": 0.758*_LEV, \"WTIOIL\": 0.906*_LEV,\n                  \"SPCX\": 0.847*_LEV, \"SP500\": 0.889*_LEV}\n     # effective: XAU 0.7653 NVDAX 0.7611 GOOGLX 0.7526 TSLAX 0.7157\n     #            AAPLX 0.8001 WTIOIL 0.9563 SPCX 0.8941 SP500 0.9384\n     VOV_MAP = {a: 0.30 for a in SCALE_MAP}\n     SEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n     CHAMPION_SPEC = (\"sv_model\", {\n         \"profile\": \"tow_full.npz\", \"seasonal\": True, \"seas_gamma\": SEAS_GAMMA,\n         \"scale\": SCALE, \"scale_map\": SCALE_MAP,\n         \"vov_map\": VOV_MAP, \"vov_halflife\": 144.0,\n         \"dist\": \"t\", \"nu\": 4.0, \"halflives\": (12.0, 72.0, 576.0),\n         \"weights\": (0.3, 0.3, 0.4), \"revert_halflife\": 96.0,\n         \"long_halflife\": 2016.0, \"winsor\": 6.0, \"pool_steps\": 4032})\n     DEFAULT_SEED = 20260914\n     def _seed(asset, start_time): # blake2b(f\"{base}|{asset}|{start_time}\")\n     ```\n     The γ comment was corrected — the 1-minute damping is now attributed to bid-ask bounce/zero-return minutes, not bucket coarseness.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/models.py`** (model zoo, HEAVILY MODIFIED). New/changed pieces:\n     ```python\n     _WEEK_MIN = 7 * 24 * 60\n     def _bidx(minutes, prof):\n         \"\"\"Bucket width read off the profile's own length, not a module constant.\"\"\"\n         return (np.asarray(minutes) % _WEEK_MIN) // (_WEEK_MIN // len(prof))\n     def _tow_index(ts0, n, step_min, prof): ...   # now takes prof\n     def _leverage_mult(u, mode, halflife, beta, cap) -> float: ...  # \"down\" / \"ret\"\n     ```\n     `sv_model` signature additions: `seas_gamma_lo`, `act_beta/act_halflives/act_cap`, `lev_beta/lev_mode/lev_halflife/lev_cap`, `vov_ar`, `vov_map`, `vov_halflife`, `vov_start`, and `scale: float | dict`. Inside `f`:\n     ```python\n     sc0 = float(scale.get(step_min, 0.9)) if isinstance(scale, dict) else float(scale)\n     sc = sc0 * (1.0 if scale_map is None else float(scale_map.get(asset, 1.0)))\n     ...\n     if lev_beta:\n         v0 *= _leverage_mult(u, lev_mode, lev_halflife, lev_beta, lev_cap)\n     ...\n     vv = vov_ar if vov_map is None else float(vov_map.get(asset, vov_ar))\n     if vv > 0 and steps > 2:\n         phi = 0.5 ** (1.0 / max(vov_halflife, 1e-9))\n         n = steps - 1\n         h = np.empty((num_simulations, n))\n         zero_start = vov_start == \"zero\"\n         h[:, 0] = 0.0 if zero_start else rng.normal(0.0, vv, size=num_simulations)\n         eps = rng.normal(0.0, vv * np.sqrt(1.0 - phi**2), size=(num_simulations, n))\n         for k in range(1, n):\n             h[:, k] = phi * h[:, k - 1] + eps[:, k]\n         var_k = (vv**2) * (1.0 - phi ** (2 * np.arange(n))) if zero_start else vv**2\n         sig = sig * np.exp(h - var_k)\n     ```\n     All defaults for `act_beta`, `lev_beta`, `seas_gamma_lo`, `vov_ar` are no-ops; `vov_map` is the only one active in the champion.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/seasonality.py`** (MODIFIED). `tow_bucket(idx, bucket_min=BUCKET_MIN)`; `fit_profile(asset, step_min, fit_end=None, smooth=5, bucket_min=BUCKET_MIN)` with `n_buckets = 7*24*60 // bucket_min`; `build(fit_end, out_name, bucket_min=BUCKET_MIN, smooth=5)`. Bug fix:\n     ```python\n     # If NO bucket cleared the threshold -- a thin asset on a fine grid, e.g. SPCX at\n     # 10-minute buckets -- there is no profile to be had and a flat one is the honest\n     # answer. Returning NaN here would silently poison every simulated price.\n     if not np.isfinite(prof).any():\n         return np.ones(n_buckets)\n     ```\n     Also carries `fit_activity()` writing `{asset}_act` into both artifacts (39 keys each; unused by champion).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_activity_crps.py`** (CREATED, was /tmp/act.py): the activity-β CRPS sweep with docstring.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_scale_1h.py`** (CREATED): global width level at the 1-minute step.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_resolution.py`** (CREATED): builds missing artifacts on demand from `GRID = ((30,5),(15,9),(15,5),(10,5),(30,3),(30,9),(60,3),(60,5))` and sweeps resolution × γ × scale; takes `1h` argv for the 1-minute leg.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_leverage.py`** (CREATED): leverage-effect sweep, both feature forms.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_vov.py`** (CREATED): within-path vol-of-vol sweep across all three legs.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/eda_activity.py`** (CREATED earlier, committed this segment).\n   - **`/workspace/agent/results_table.py`** (MODIFIED): now takes optional argv `[champion.json] [baseline.json]`, defaulting to `off_champ.json`/`off_base.json`.\n   - **`/workspace/agent/journal.md`**: Iters 0–18 (14 activity, 15 resolution, 16 leverage, 17 champion change, 18 follow-ups).\n   - **`/workspace/agent/report.md`**: §3 updated with `m_k` term and `scale(asset, step)`; §4 gained \"Fattening the aggregated intervals (−0.10 % on com-equ, three windows)\"; §5 gained \"A finer time-of-week grid\" and \"Trade count and volume: real regression signal, zero CRPS\" plus a vol-of-vol footnote; §7 gained a caveat that the last two parameters had no untouched window left; §8 renumbered to 6 items with a new item 5 on shape; §9 lists all experiment scripts. **§6 results tables still hold the OLD champion's numbers and must be regenerated.**\n   - **Artifacts**: only `tow_full.npz`, `tow_pre0701.npz`, `volfit_full.npz`, `volfit_pre0701.npz` remain; all scratch resolution artifacts were deleted (rebuildable via `exp_resolution.py`).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n\n   - **vov patch landed in the wrong function.** `shocks = np.zeros((num_simulations, steps))` occurs 3× in `models.py`; a `.replace(..., 1)` hit an earlier model that uses `sigma` not `sig`. Symptom: bit-identical sweep results across every vov setting. First fix attempt also failed because `assert s.count(anchor) == 1` on the `vol_of_vol` block was false (it appears twice). Fixed by slicing between `\\ndef sv_model(` and the next `\\ndef ` and editing only inside that slice. Verified afterwards: 24h kurtosis 3.25 → 4.57 at sd=0.5, 5-min sd unchanged to 6 digits.\n   - **Garbled \"ret\" leverage feature**: first version had `** 0.0` and a double division. Rewritten as a proper z-score: `se = rms*sqrt(Σw²)/Σw; x = clip(-m/se, -4, 4)`. Verified mean≈0, sd≈1.0 under symmetric noise.\n   - **All-NaN profile**: at 10-minute buckets SPCX had no bucket ≥20 observations, so `np.nanmedian` of an all-NaN array produced a silently all-NaN profile that would have served NaN prices. Fixed with the flat-profile fallback above.\n   - **First official-eval launch was mis-detached**: I used `( ... ) &` inside a `run_in_background` Bash call; the tool reported exit 0 after 5 s while the job actually kept running. Confirmed alive via `pgrep`. The second launch used `setsid nohup ... < /dev/null &`.\n   - **Killing the eval left an orphan**: `pkill -f official_eval` killed the scripts but a running `predict.py --asset HYPE` survived; cleared with `pkill -9 -f \"agent/predict.py\"`.\n   - **Crypto baseline looked inconsistent** between a sweep table and a direct run (3856.579 vs 3864.532): the sweep's baseline row was itself `min` over the scale grid. Resolved by re-testing at the level each configuration actually ships at — which confirmed the crypto sign flip is real, not a grid artefact.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Shipped (champion changed twice this segment, both at commit `e965c35`):**\n   - `vov_map` = 0.30 for the 8 com-equ assets, `vov_halflife` 144: −0.096/−0.096/−0.102% on three disjoint windows; all 24 per-asset×window cells negative. Carries a uniform level correction `_LEV = 0.95/0.90` on `SCALE_MAP`.\n   - `scale` keyed on step size `{5: 0.90, 1: 0.95}`: −0.085/−0.215/−0.049% on crypto-1h across three windows; crypto-24h flips sign so 0.90 stays.\n   - Served interface re-verified offline from `/tmp`: no chdir, no synth_lib/harness import, correct shapes for both horizons on a NaN-bearing context, seed-reproducible across reloads, different seed → different paths, 0.053 s/prompt (24h) and 0.015 s (1h) at 1000 paths.\n\n   **Rejected on evidence this segment:** the bounded activity multiplier (every β worse, monotonically); finer *and* coarser time-of-week resolution; the leverage effect in both standard forms; `vov_start=\"zero\"` (a tie); vov for crypto (sign flip at the shipping level); `nu` ≠ 4 with the factor on.\n\n   **Commits this segment:** `5c53921` (activity), `10bfa18` (resolution + NaN fix), `cc08cef` (leverage), `e965c35` (champion change), `93103ec` (Iter 18 follow-ups).\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n   - A continuation instruction to resume from the prior summary without recapping or prefacing.\n   - The final message instructing that this summary be produced as text only, with no tool calls.\n   - All other inserted blocks were automated `<task-notification>` background-task events explicitly marked NOT user input, system reminders that files changed on disk, a system-reminder directing Bash-first tool usage under bypass permissions mode, and a git-attribution reminder requiring commit messages to end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>` and PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. No other user-role messages exist.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - Wait for the running official evaluation (18 legs, `/workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ2.json`, log `/tmp/off2.log`) to finish; **do not edit `models.py` or `modeling.py` while it runs** — each leg is a fresh process that re-imports them.\n   - Regenerate report §6 tables with `uv run python agent/results_table.py off_champ2.json off_base.json` and patch `report.md`.\n   - Re-read `agent/BUDGET.md` at the start of each iteration; honour any LANDING ORDER immediately.\n   - **Create `agent/CHAMPION` LAST** (YAML: `sha` = an existing git commit — `93103ec` or later, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles: [low, high]`, `notes` containing backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS). MANDATORY — no CHAMPION = Score 0 — but **nominating is final**, so write it only after everything else is committed and verified.\n   - Keep the report's caveat that `tow_full.npz` and the com-equ map include the backtested windows, so §6 is mildly optimistic relative to §4–§5.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   Immediately before this summary request I had: (a) frozen the champion after Iteration 18's two negative follow-ups, (b) written journal Iter 18 and committed it as `93103ec`, (c) relaunched the definitive 18-leg official evaluation detached:\n   ```\n   setsid nohup bash -c 'bash agent/official_eval.sh agent /workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ2.json /tmp/off2.log && bash agent/official_eval_1h.sh agent /workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ2.json /tmp/off2.log' > /tmp/off2.run 2>&1 < /dev/null &\n   ```\n   confirmed launched via `pgrep -f official_eval`, and (d) read BUDGET.md: 50.34/100 USD, 7.2 h elapsed, 10.8 h remaining, phase normal.\n\n   The official run takes roughly 12–15 minutes per asset (~3.5 h for all 18 legs). The starting-point numbers to compare against are already in `miner_outputs/off_base.json`; the previous champion's official results were CRYPTO_24H 3527.7 vs 3680.1 (−4.14%), COM_EQU_24H 1824.9 vs 2076.5 (−12.11%), CRYPTO_1H 799.5 vs 831.9 (−3.90%). crypto-24h should come back bit-identical to the previous champion since neither new change touches it; com-equ-24h should improve ~0.1% and crypto-1h ~0.05–0.2%.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Wait for the official evaluation to complete (monitoring `/tmp/off2.log` for the 18 `ok` lines and the `DONE-1H` marker), then regenerate the §6 tables and finish the deliverables. Verbatim from my last actions: *\"Launching the definitive official run now, since it's the long pole\"* and, from the pending-task list, *\"**Create `agent/CHAMPION` LAST** ... This is MANDATORY — no CHAMPION = Score 0 — but **nominating is final**, so it must be written only after everything else is committed and verified.\"*\n\n   Concretely: (1) confirm all 18 legs succeeded with no `Read-only file system` errors (the 24h legs end 2026-09-13 and the 1h leg 2026-09-12 precisely to avoid the backtester's +26 h price request crossing the snapshot edge); (2) run `uv run python agent/results_table.py off_champ2.json off_base.json` and patch report §6; (3) commit; (4) write `agent/CHAMPION` with `sha` set to the final commit and `notes` carrying the per-configuration champion and starting-point CRPS.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"7907231c-b788-42db-ac01-eb6a8bef9ef4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T00:15:02.514Z","isSynthetic":true}
