{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYfPEjGsgFhidU7P7KMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XLzgQsdC52i5Nvn4dp2DqB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"agent/report.md\"); s = p.read_text()\n\nold = \"\"\"6. **Re-audit every other parameter the way γ was re-audited.** γ was chosen by a 1-D sweep that\n   was silently measuring the level. `revert_halflife`, the EWMA half-lives and the winsorisation\n   threshold were all chosen the same way. Only γ has been re-checked with the level free.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"6. **Model the `*_gaps` block in CRYPTO_1H explicitly.** Twelve of that configuration's terms\n   are cumulative returns from the prompt start rather than interval returns — about 29 % of its\n   budget — and they are far more correlated with each other than the interval terms are, because\n   they share an endpoint. Nothing in this model knows that; the gaps are whatever the path\n   generator happens to emit. A width that is fitted per *term type* rather than per step size is\n   the largest piece of structure in the scoring rule I never touched.\n7. **Find more forward-looking information.** The framing in §5 says the only features that can\n   pay are the ones a fast EWMA cannot already see, and the time-of-week profile is the crudest\n   possible version of that: it knows the US cash open happens every weekday, but not that this\n   particular Wednesday carries a CPI print or an NVDA earnings date. A scheduled-event calendar\n   is the obvious next one — and it is the only idea on this list that is *certain* not to be\n   redundant with what the model already has.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1; s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = \"\"\"uv run python agent/results_table.py                              # renders the tables in §6\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"uv run python agent/results_table.py off_champ.json off_base.json # renders the 