{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYfr2RMs4Zy8vaePTLYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SrvkjtpfLq44JW9uaQcvs8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"agent/suggestions.md\"); s = p.read_text()\na = s.index(\"13. **The `*_gaps` block in CRYPTO_1H.**\")\nb = s.index(\"14. **Scheduled events.**\")\nnew = '''13. ~~**The `*_gaps` block in CRYPTO_1H.**~~ Tested and closed (Iteration 20). Off the round\n    hour the gaps ladder is dispersed at or slightly below the interval ladder, so the twelve\n    cumulative-return terms are already paid for by the terms that share their horizon. What is\n    worth carrying forward is the trap: **do not run a calibration diagnostic on a prompt grid\n    whose cadence divides an hour.** A 180-minute cadence lands on :00 every time, and the\n    round-hour volatility spike then shows up as a clean 28 % under-dispersion on the first five\n    minutes of every path, in every asset. It is entirely an artifact — 173 or 97 minutes makes\n    it vanish. Comparing two models on such a grid is fine, because the bias cancels; measuring\n    an absolute calibration level on it is not.\n\n'''\np.write_text(s[:a] + new + s[b:])\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ngit -C /workspace add -A agent/suggestions.md && git -C /workspace commit -q -m \"Suggestions: close the gaps-block idea, keep the round-hour trap\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && echo ok; tail -1 /tmp/off2.log","description":"Update suggestions and commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":85107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1787,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},