not be worth more than a rounding error.","+","+### Refitting the per-asset multipliers against the shipped configuration","+","+The eight com-equ multipliers were fitted when the champion had a different seasonal exponent and","+no vol-of-vol factor; when the factor landed I corrected the whole map by one uniform number.","+Eight assets with different seasonal amplitudes should not share a correction, so I refit all eight","+against the champion's own gamma, factor and profile, on a window preceding every validation","+window. Every multiplier moved down by 0.04–0.09 — very nearly a constant offset in logs, i.e. a","+*level*, which §2 says is nearly free and which the level sweep absorbs. Out of sample the refit","+map is within 0.06 % of the shipped one and disagrees in sign across windows. The shape of the map","+is what generalises; its position was already right.","+"," ### The `*_gaps` block in CRYPTO_1H — and a clock that nearly fooled me"," "," Twelve of the eighteen interval terms in the 1-hour configuration are the cumulative return from"]},{"oldStart":560,"oldLines":6,"newStart":600,"newLines":9,"lines":[" uv run python agent/exp_vov.py                      # §4: the AR(1) vol-of-vol factor"," uv run python agent/eda_gaps.py                     # §5: per-term dispersion, CRYPTO_1H"," uv run python agent/verify_floor.py                 # §7: the volatility floor never binds","+uv run python agent/exp_ramp.py                     # §5: the horizon width ramp","+uv run python agent/exp_gamma_regime.py             # §5: calendar x regime interaction","+uv run python agent/exp_recalibrate.py check        # §5: refit the com-equ multipliers"," ```"," "," `agent/harness.py` + `agent/evaluate.py` + `agent/sweep.py` are the fast iteration loop — 545"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/workspace/agent/journal.md","/workspace/agent/report.md"]}}}
