{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single genuine user message in the entire conversation was: **\"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"** (plus a continuation instruction to resume from a prior summary without recapping, and the final instruction to produce this summary as text only).\n\n   `/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md` is the campaign constitution:\n   - **Objective**: build the price-simulation model with the lowest **CRPS** (lower = better) for Synth Bittensor subnet SN50, across three scoring configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP/HYPE, 86400s/300s, 289 pts), COM_EQU_24H (XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX/TSLAX/AAPLX/WTIOIL/SPCX/SP500, 86400s/300s), CRYPTO_1H (crypto, 3600s/60s, 61 pts). 1000 simulations per prompt; honour whatever `num_simulations` is passed.\n   - **Judge every experiment on CRPS**, per configuration and per asset. \"Never trade a CRPS regression for a better one.\"\n   - Champion is evaluated over the **10 days following the 2026-09-14 data cutoff**.\n   - Work solo; no one can answer questions; record decisions in the journal.\n   - **Envelope**: 100.00 USD credits, 18h wall-clock. Read `agent/BUDGET.md` **at the start of each iteration**; a LANDING ORDER there is non-negotiable.\n   - **\"Nominating is final** — the first time you stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, your campaign is over: you will not be resumed, and every remaining dollar and hour is forfeited. Until then you may keep iterating and amend your nomination. Nominate early only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score. **A champion is MANDATORY.** What is scored is how strong your champion is, not whether you dared to nominate one: ending with no `agent/CHAMPION` is a Score of 0 and a wasted leg — strictly worse than nominating something imperfect.\"\n   - **Hardware**: GCP g2-standard-16, 14 CPU / 48GB RAM / 1× NVIDIA L4; only one GPU job at a time.\n\n   **Constraints stated verbatim in CAMPAIGN.md that MUST continue to apply:**\n   1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat everything after **2026-09-14** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and invalidates the result. Audited on your transcript.\n   2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges, aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n   3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester` (via `agent/predict.py`). One implementation of the metric is what makes results comparable. NEVER reimplement the metric.\n   4. Not allowed: falsifying the journal or results; reproducing another participant's served output as your own.\n   5. **Keep binary and encoded data out of your terminal output.** Read parquet with pandas and `.npy` with numpy — never `cat` a parquet, a git bundle, or model weights, and never pipe base64 into your context.\n   6. **Start from public sources only**: synth-lib, synth-subnet, the Synth API, and your own ideas. The operator's existing miner models are not part of your materials and must not inform your work; if any turns up, leave it unread and note it in `suggestions.md`.\n   7. Final champion must expose in `agent/modeling.py`: `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` -> `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`, each path `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context. `context_prices` is a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days preceding `start_time` with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`; it MAY CONTAIN NaN — **drop, never interpolate**. Must run OFFLINE.\n   8. **If the model uses randomness, seed it from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`** — read once at the top of `simulate()`, seed every generator; fall back to a chosen seed when absent.\n   - Operational rules: always run commands from the workspace root; `market_data/` is READ-ONLY; run everything through `uv run`; don't backtest across the three structural breaks (2026-06-23 competition split, 2026-03-11 crypto-1h formula change, ~2026-07-17 SPYX retired / SP500 introduced — **SPYX is DEAD**).\n\n   **Required deliverables (in `agent/`, in English, committed to git):** `journal.md` (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson per iteration), `report.md` (explainer style for Synth miners), `CHAMPION` (YAML: `sha` = an EXISTING git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles` `[low, high]`, `notes` MUST include backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS; \"The harness checks the interface as soon as this file appears (result in BUDGET.md) — fix it if the check fails\"), `suggestions.md`.\n\n   **Mid-conversation system instruction (still in effect):** while bypass permissions mode is active, do work through the Bash tool wherever it can accomplish the job (cat/sed/grep/heredocs/short scripts) rather than the dedicated Read/Edit/Write tools; fall back to a dedicated tool only when Bash genuinely cannot do the job.\n\n   **Git attribution reminder (still in effect):** end git commit messages with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`; end PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **CRPS decomposition**: validator score = sum of **univariate** CRPS terms on relative price changes over intervals, in bps. No multivariate term. 24h: 5min 288 terms ≈61%, 30min 48 ≈25%, 3hour 8 ≈10%, 24hour_abs 1 ≈3.6%. CRYPTO_1H intervals (verified this session): `{'1min':60,'2min':120,'5min':300,'15min':900,'30min':1800,'60min_abs':3600,'0_5min_gaps':300,'0_10min_gaps':600,...,'0_60min_gaps':3600}` plus `vol_scoring_blocks {'vol_60min':(3600,1.75),'vol_15min':(900,0.4375),'vol_5min':(300,0.1458)}`. The 24h competitions have **empty** `vol_scoring_blocks` (confirmed).\n   - **The central identity**: `E CRPS(σ) = sqrt(2/π)·sqrt(1+σ²) − σ/sqrt(π)`, minimised at σ=1; `E CRPS(σ)/E CRPS(1) ≈ 1 + 0.25·(log σ)²`. A constant scale error is nearly free; the entire recoverable CRPS is `Var(log σ̂ − log σ_true)`. Asymmetry: too wide grows linearly, too narrow saturates at +41%, so the CRPS-optimal width sits slightly below `exp(E[log σ])`.\n   - **The oracle gap**: ≈6% better than the causal champion on crypto-24h — bounds the level-forecasting pot.\n   - **The level confound (Iter 12)**: sweep shape parameters with the level re-optimised at every point.\n   - **The transfer criterion**: parameter stability under refitting predicts out-of-sample transfer better than in-sample gain. Effects under ~0.1%, or disagreeing in sign between windows, are noise.\n   - **The redundancy principle (Iter 16)**: range estimators, trade activity and leverage all failed because each acts on future volatility *through* realized volatility, which a fast EWMA already prices in. Only forward-looking (scheduled) information can be incremental.\n   - **Shape vs level (Iter 17)**: ~39% of a 24h score is on aggregated intervals; a deterministic σ path makes those too Gaussian by the CLT. An AR(1) factor in log-vol renormalised to preserve each step's variance exactly fattens the aggregates without disturbing the 61%.\n   - **NEW — the round-hour prompt-grid artifact (Iter 20)**: a cadence dividing an hour always lands on :00; the round-hour volatility spike then masquerades as a 28% under-dispersion on the first five minutes of every path. Harmless when comparing two models (bias cancels), fatal for an absolute calibration diagnostic.\n   - **NEW — right sign, third-order size (Iters 22-23)**: two structurally-motivated shape knobs both fitted with the sign theory predicts and a magnitude an order of magnitude below the 0.1% threshold — evidence the model sits at the bottom of a flat basin.\n   - Three validation windows: **dev** 2026-07-05..07-23, **val3** 2026-07-24..08-25, **test** 2026-08-26..09-13 (1h test ends 09-12).\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/BUDGET.md`** (harness-maintained, read-only). Last read: `Credits: 61.46 / 100.00 USD (61%)`, `Time: 8.6 h elapsed, 9.4 h remaining (48%)`, `Phase: normal`. **Must be re-read at the start of each iteration.**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/modeling.py`** (champion entry point). Current CHAMPION_SPEC (formatting is one key per line):\n     ```python\n     CHAMPION_SPEC = (\n         \"sv_model\",\n         {\n             \"profile\": \"tow_full.npz\",\n             \"seasonal\": True,\n             \"seas_gamma\": SEAS_GAMMA,          # {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n             \"scale\": SCALE,                    # {5: 0.90, 1: 0.95}\n             \"scale_map\": SCALE_MAP,            # per-asset, includes _LEV = 0.95/0.90\n             \"vov_map\": VOV_MAP,                # {a: 0.30 for the 8 com-equ assets}\n             \"vov_halflife\": 144.0,\n             # Insurance only: a floor on the conditional level, ~7x below the quietest level any\n             # real prompt in the snapshot produces. Verified never to bind\n             # (agent/verify_floor.py), so the measured numbers are unaffected; it exists so that\n             # a halted venue -- seven days of identical closes -- cannot make the model serve an\n             # almost degenerate distribution.\n             \"vol_floor\": 1.5e-5,\n             \"dist\": \"t\",\n             \"nu\": 4.0,\n             \"halflives\": (12.0, 72.0, 576.0),\n             \"weights\": (0.3, 0.3, 0.4),\n             \"revert_halflife\": 96.0,\n             \"long_halflife\": 2016.0,\n             \"winsor\": 6.0,\n             \"pool_steps\": 4032,\n         },\n     )\n     DEFAULT_SEED = 20260914\n     ```\n     Effective SCALE_MAP values (already include `_LEV`): XAU 0.765, NVDAX 0.761, GOOGLX 0.753, TSLAX 0.716, AAPLX 0.800, WTIOIL 0.956, SPCX 0.894, SP500 0.938 — range 0.72–0.96. `_seed(asset, start_time)` uses blake2b over `f\"{base}|{asset}|{start_time}\"` with base from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED` or `DEFAULT_SEED`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/models.py`** (model zoo). `MIN_SIGMA = 1e-6` at line 14. New `sv_model` parameters added this session (all defaulting to no-ops except `vol_floor` which the champion sets):\n     ```python\n     scale_map=None,   # per-asset multiplier on top of `scale`, fitted out-of-sample\n     # Absolute floor on the conditional (deseasonalised) level, in per-step return units.\n     # Insurance against a degenerate context, not a modelling choice -- see below. 0 disables it.\n     vol_floor: float = 0.0,\n     # Tilts the width linearly across the horizon at constant mean: >0 widens late steps and\n     # narrows early ones, <0 the reverse. A pure shape knob -- the ramp is renormalised to mean 1\n     # so it cannot move the level, which is swept separately (journal Iter 12). 0 disables it.\n     scale_ramp: float = 0.0,\n     # Interaction between the calendar and the current regime. The seasonal exponent becomes\n     # gamma + seas_gamma_beta * log(v0 / v_long), so a negative beta flattens the time-of-week\n     # profile when the market is hot relative to its own week. 0 disables it.\n     seas_gamma_beta: float = 0.0,\n     # Shrink the reversion target toward a committed per-asset long-run level (vlong.py). The\n     # context is only 7 days, so a week that happened to be hot leaves a target that is itself an\n     # overshoot; the artifact is the one piece of information about the asset that is NOT in the\n     # context. 0 disables it and the target stays the context's own level.\n     vlong_art: str | None = None,\n     long_blend: float = 0.0,\n     ```\n     Factory-time loading:\n     ```python\n     _vlong = None\n     if long_blend and vlong_art:\n         import vlong as _vl0\n         _vlong = _vl0.load(vlong_art)\n     ```\n     Inside `f`, the v0/v_long block now reads:\n     ```python\n     if lev_beta:\n         v0 *= _leverage_mult(u, lev_mode, lev_halflife, lev_beta, lev_cap)\n     # A context in which every close is identical -- a halted or delisted venue, seven\n     # days of it -- drives the EWMA down to MIN_SIGMA, which is a numerical guard and not\n     # a forecast: the model would serve a distribution ~75x narrower than the quietest\n     # real prompt in the snapshot, and CRPS is unbounded above when the truth then moves.\n     # The floor caps that loss. It sits well below any level a live asset produces and is\n     # verified never to bind (agent/verify_floor.py), so it costs exactly nothing.\n     v0 = max(v0, vol_floor)\n     if revert_halflife > 0:\n         _vl = float(_ewma_var_multi(u2, [long_halflife])[0])\n         v_long = max(_vl if est == \"mad\" else np.sqrt(max(_vl, MIN_SIGMA**2)),\n                      MIN_SIGMA, vol_floor)\n         if _vlong is not None:\n             vb = _vlong.get(f\"{asset}_{step_min}\")\n             if vb:\n                 v_long = float(np.exp((1.0 - long_blend) * np.log(v_long)\n                                       + long_blend * np.log(vb)))\n         k = np.arange(1, steps)\n         phi = 0.5 ** (k / revert_halflife)\n         v_k = np.exp(np.log(v_long) + phi * (np.log(v0) - np.log(v_long)))\n     else:\n         v_k = np.full(steps - 1, v0)\n     if seas_gamma_beta and seasonal and revert_halflife > 0:\n         # Story: a macro shock does not respect trading hours, so in a hot regime the\n         # overnight buckets catch up and the day/night ratio compresses. The profile's\n         # SHAPE is the only thing that moves -- `_bend` renormalises to mean 1 -- so this\n         # cannot smuggle in a level change.\n         praw = prof_raw.get(f\"{asset}_{step_min}\")\n         if praw is not None:\n             g0 = (float(_gammas.get(step_min, 1.0)) if _gammas is not None\n                   else float(seas_gamma))\n             z = float(np.clip(np.log(v0 / v_long), -1.5, 1.5))\n             ge = float(np.clip(g0 + seas_gamma_beta * z, 0.2, 2.5))\n             s_fut = _bend(praw, ge, ge)[fut_b]\n     sigma_path = v_k * s_fut\n     ```\n     and after the level multiplier:\n     ```python\n     sigma_path = np.maximum(sigma_path, MIN_SIGMA) * sc\n     if scale_ramp:\n         ramp = 1.0 + scale_ramp * (np.arange(steps - 1) / max(steps - 2, 1))\n         sigma_path = sigma_path * (ramp / ramp.mean())\n     ```\n     Key existing helpers: `_bend(v, g_hi, g_lo)` raises the profile to `g_hi` above 1 and `g_lo` below, then renormalises to mean 1; `_profile_for(step_min)` caches bent profiles; `sc0 = float(scale.get(step_min, 0.9)) if isinstance(scale, dict) else float(scale)`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/vlong.py`** (CREATED this session). Builds `vlong_pre0701.npz` and `vlong_full.npz` (26 levels each = 13 assets × steps 1 and 5). Statistic must match `v_long` exactly: RMS of winsorised log returns at the step, deseasonalised by the SAME bent time-of-week profile. `_bend(v, g) = (v**g)/(v**g).mean()`; `fit_level(asset, step_min, prof, gamma, fit_end, winsor=6.0)`; `build(fit_end, tow_name, out_name, gammas)`; `load(name)`. `__main__` builds both from `SEAS_GAMMA`. Sample values: BTC 5-min 1.22e-03 / 1-min 5.26e-04; NVDAX 1.01e-03 / 4.26e-04; SP500 4.01e-04 / 1.60e-04.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/eda_gaps.py`** (CREATED). Per-term dispersion diagnostic for CRYPTO_1H. `CADENCES = (173, 97, 180)`; `_terms(paths, name, seconds, ti)` returns cumulative-from-start for `*_gaps` and strided non-overlapping returns otherwise; `ratios(model, cadence)` returns mean|realized| / mean|simulated| per term. Docstring records the RMS→mean-absolute switch and the round-hour warning.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/verify_floor.py`** (CREATED). Asserts the champion is bit-identical with and without `vol_floor` across `WINDOWS` × all 13 assets × both horizons (cadence 180 for 24h, 173 for 1h), 8 sims per prompt, `np.array_equal`. Output: \"9802 prompts, all bit-identical with and without the floor. floor = 1.50e-05; the quietest prompt's served per-step sd is 3.3x it.\"\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_ramp.py`** (CREATED). `RAMPS = (-0.30,-0.15,0.0,0.15,0.30)`, `LEVELS = (0.90,0.95,1.00)`, `LEGS = ((\"comequ-24h\",\"comequ\",86400,300),(\"crypto-24h\",\"crypto\",86400,300),(\"crypto-1h\",\"crypto\",3600,60))`, `kw = dict(base, profile=\"tow_pre0701.npz\")`, 500 sims, cadence 180, min over level grid.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_gamma_regime.py`** (CREATED, sed-derived from exp_ramp.py). `BETAS = (-1.0,-0.5,0.0,0.5,1.0)`, `seas_gamma_beta=r`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_recalibrate.py`** (CREATED). `FIT_EARLY = [(\"2026-05-20\",\"2026-06-20\")]`, `FIT_SHIP = [(\"2026-08-01\",\"2026-09-13\")]`; argv `check` (default) or `ship`; pops `scale_map` and `scale` from the champion kwargs before calling `calibrate()`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/exp_vlong.py`** (CREATED). `BLENDS = (0.0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8)`, `kw = dict(base, profile=\"tow_pre0701.npz\", vlong_art=\"vlong_pre0701.npz\")`, otherwise identical structure to exp_ramp.py.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/journal.md`**: Iterations 0–24. New this session: 19 (dynamics re-audit, null), 20 (gaps block + round-hour artifact), 21 (vol floor, kept), 22 (horizon ramp, rejected), 23 (calendar×regime, rejected), 24 (refit multipliers, rejected).\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/report.md`** (475+ lines, 9 sections). §6 now carries the final official tables. New §5 subsections: \"The leverage effect\", \"Why those three failures are the same failure\", \"The `*_gaps` block in CRYPTO_1H — and a clock that nearly fooled me\", \"Two shape knobs with the right sign and the wrong size\", \"Refitting the per-asset multipliers against the shipped configuration\". §7 gained the halted-venue limitation. §8 is now 7 items ending with \"Find more forward-looking information\". §9 lists all experiment scripts.\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/suggestions.md`**: items 1-9 (harness/predict.py/scoring), 10 (cross-asset pooling — corrected to say it is NOT servable), 11, 12, 13 (struck through, round-hour trap), 14 (scheduled events), 16 (the redundancy principle, own section), 17-18 (process).\n\n   - **`/tmp/snap.py`** (scratch): generates a 23200-float fingerprint of `simulate()` across 4 (asset, ti, tl) combos on a fixed NaN-bearing context, for bit-identity checks via `git stash`/`git stash pop`.\n\n   - **Artifacts**: `tow_full.npz`, `tow_pre0701.npz`, `volfit_full.npz`, `volfit_pre0701.npz`, and NEW `vlong_full.npz`, `vlong_pre0701.npz`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/miner_outputs/off_champ2.json`** (18 legs, final champion) — also copied to `off_champ.json`. `off_base.json` is the starting point.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - `mod, fac, kw = CHAMPION_SPEC` → `ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 3, got 2)`. `CHAMPION_SPEC` is `(factory_name, kwargs)`. Fixed with `sed -i 's/    mod, fac, kw = CHAMPION_SPEC/    fac, kw = CHAMPION_SPEC/'`.\n   - Patching `modeling.py` with the anchor `'\"dist\": \"t\", \"nu\": 4.0, \"halflives\": (12.0, 72.0, 576.0),'` raised AssertionError because the real file has one key per line. Fixed by printing the actual `CHAMPION_SPEC` block with `sed -n '/^CHAMPION_SPEC/,/^})/p'` and anchoring on `'\"vov_halflife\": 144.0,\\n        \"dist\": \"t\",'`.\n   - `sleep 900; tail ...` and `sleep 120; cat ...` were both **blocked by the harness**: \"To wait for a condition, use Monitor with an until-loop... To wait for a command you started, use run_in_background: true. Do not chain shorter sleeps to work around this block.\" Switched to `until <cond>; do sleep N; done` with `run_in_background: true` or a 600s timeout.\n   - The first `eda_gaps.py` pass used a 180-minute cadence and an RMS ratio, producing a spurious 28% under-dispersion on `0_5min_gaps`. Diagnosed as a round-hour artifact (confirmed by re-running at 173 and 97 minutes) and a tail-dominated statistic (confirmed by the pooled level moving 10 points between grids). Fixed by sweeping three cadences and switching to a mean-absolute ratio.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Shipped this session:** only `vol_floor = 1.5e-5` (Iteration 21), verified bit-identical over 9802 real prompts so the official numbers stand unmodified.\n\n   **Rejected on evidence this session:** all alternative dynamics knobs re-audited with the factor on (Iter 19); a per-term width for the CRYPTO_1H gaps block (Iter 20 — no seam exists); the horizon width ramp (Iter 22); the calendar × regime interaction on the seasonal exponent (Iter 23); refitting the com-equ multipliers against the shipping configuration (Iter 24).\n\n   **Official evaluation completed** (18/18 legs `ok`, no read-only-filesystem errors): CRYPTO_24H 3527.7 vs 3680.1 (−4.14%), COM_EQU_24H 1822.5 vs 2076.5 (−12.23%), CRYPTO_1H 798.7 vs 831.9 (−4.00%). Ahead on all 18 asset/configuration combinations. Tables patched into report §6.\n\n   **Commits this session:** `cd29c92` (Iter 19), plus commits for the suggestions rewrite and the cross-asset correction, `d2bd722` (Iter 20), `2f4e611` (official results), `cab0cb4` (Iter 21 floor), `fb518ff` (Iter 22 ramp), `e4f913b` (Iters 23-24).\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n   - A continuation instruction to resume from the prior summary without recapping or prefacing.\n   - The final message instructing that this summary be produced as text only, with no tool calls.\n   - All other inserted blocks were automated `<task-notification>` background-task events explicitly marked NOT user input, system reminders that files changed on disk, a system-reminder directing Bash-first tool usage under bypass permissions mode, and a git-attribution reminder. No other user-role messages exist.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - **Finish Iteration 25 (the `long_blend` sweep just returned results).** The com-equ leg shows `long_blend = 0.2` at **−0.171 / −0.041 / −0.037 %** — negative on all three windows, ~−0.08 % mean, the first candidate in many iterations to clear that bar. crypto-24h flips sign (dev +0.026 / val3 +0.021 / test −0.145 at 0.2; +0.120/+0.113/−0.215 at 0.4) and crypto-1h is mixed (−0.040/+0.002/−0.024 at 0.2). Decide whether to ship `long_blend = 0.2` for com-equ only (matching the vov precedent), re-optimise the level at the shipped point per Iter 18's rule, journal it, and — if shipped — rebuild/keep `vlong_full.npz` for serving and re-run the affected official legs.\n   - Re-read `agent/BUDGET.md` at the start of each iteration; honour any LANDING ORDER immediately.\n   - If the champion changes, re-run `agent/official_eval.sh` / `official_eval_1h.sh` for the affected legs and regenerate report §6 with `uv run python agent/results_table.py <champ>.json off_base.json`.\n   - Add `agent/vlong.py` and `agent/exp_vlong.py` to report §9 and a §5 (or §4) subsection for Iteration 25.\n   - **Create `agent/CHAMPION` LAST** (YAML: `sha` = an existing git commit — `e4f913b` or later, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles: [low, high]`, `notes` containing backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS). MANDATORY — no CHAMPION = Score 0 — but **nominating is final**, so write it only after everything else is committed and verified. Because \"the harness checks the interface as soon as this file appears (result in BUDGET.md)\", the plan is to write CHAMPION and then poll `agent/BUDGET.md` for the interface-check result **within the same turn** (a bash `until` loop, never stopping) and fix any failure before stopping.\n   - Keep the report's caveat that `tow_full.npz` and the com-equ map include the backtested windows, so §6 is mildly optimistic relative to §4–§5.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   Immediately before this summary request I was running **Iteration 25 — should the reversion target be shrunk toward a committed long-run level?** I had:\n   - created `agent/vlong.py` and built `vlong_pre0701.npz` / `vlong_full.npz` (26 levels each);\n   - added `vlong_art` and `long_blend` to `sv_model` (both default no-ops);\n   - created `agent/exp_vlong.py` and run it in the background.\n\n   The sweep completed with (% vs `long_blend = 0`, each cell the minimum over the level grid (0.90, 0.95, 1.00), `profile=\"tow_pre0701.npz\"`, `vlong_art=\"vlong_pre0701.npz\"`, 500 sims, cadence 180):\n\n   ```\n   ### comequ-24h            dev_%  val3_%  test_%\n   0.2                      -0.171  -0.041  -0.037\n   0.4                      -0.254  -0.020  +0.041\n   0.6                      -0.250  +0.065  +0.251\n   0.8                      -0.161  +0.210  +0.614\n   ### crypto-24h\n   0.2                      +0.026  +0.021  -0.145\n   0.4                      +0.120  +0.113  -0.215\n   0.6                      +0.287  +0.286  -0.212\n   0.8                      +0.533  +0.632  -0.138\n   ### crypto-1h\n   0.2                      -0.040  +0.002  -0.024\n   0.4                      -0.071  +0.029  -0.042\n   0.6                      -0.091  +0.081  -0.053\n   0.8                      -0.122  +0.161  -0.057\n   ```\n\n   No journal entry, report update, or commit has been made for Iteration 25 yet; the champion is currently unchanged (`long_blend` defaults to 0, so `CHAMPION_SPEC` is untouched and the official numbers in §6 remain valid).\n\n   Budget at last read: 61.46/100 USD (61%), 8.6 h elapsed, 9.4 h remaining (48%), Phase normal. Latest commit `e4f913b`.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Evaluate whether `long_blend = 0.2` should ship for the com-equ assets only. The com-equ row is the first result in many iterations that is negative on all three disjoint windows (−0.171 / −0.041 / −0.037 %), while crypto-24h shows the same sign flip that kept the vov factor off for crypto (dev/val3 positive, test negative) and crypto-1h is inconsistent. This exactly mirrors the precedent already in the journal for `vov_map`: ship the effect for com-equ, leave crypto alone.\n\n   Concretely, per the rule established in Iteration 18 and restated in the Iteration 24 journal entry — *\"Iter 18's lesson was to evaluate at the configuration you would actually serve\"* — the next step is to re-test `long_blend = 0.2` for com-equ **at the level the configuration actually ships at** (`scale = {5: 0.90}` with the existing `SCALE_MAP`) rather than at the minimum over a level grid, check whether the gain survives and whether it carries a level correction the way the vov factor did, and only then decide. If it survives, add `vlong_art=\"vlong_full.npz\"` and a per-asset/`comequ`-only `long_blend` to `CHAMPION_SPEC`, journal Iteration 25, update report §4/§9, commit, and re-run the eight com-equ official legs before touching `agent/CHAMPION`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"31bd8e3f-6103-4faa-aa54-41c41a3795ea","timestamp":"2026-09-30T01:41:28.472Z","isSynthetic":true}
