ommitted`. `fit_end` lets a","+window be scored against a level fitted strictly before it. `agent/exp_vlong.py` sweeps b.","+","+**Result**. Sweep over b, each cell the minimum over the level grid, 500 paths, artifact fitted","+through 2026-06-30 (before all three windows), % vs b=0:","+","+| b | com-equ dev | val3 | test | crypto-24h dev | val3 | test | crypto-1h dev | val3 | test |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| 0.2 | −0.171 | −0.041 | −0.037 | +0.026 | +0.021 | −0.145 | −0.040 | +0.002 | −0.024 |","+| 0.4 | −0.254 | −0.020 | +0.041 | +0.120 | +0.113 | −0.215 | −0.071 | +0.029 | −0.042 |","+| 0.6 | −0.250 | +0.065 | +0.251 | +0.287 | +0.286 | −0.212 | −0.091 | +0.081 | −0.053 |","+| 0.8 | −0.161 | +0.210 | +0.614 | +0.533 | +0.632 | −0.122 | +0.161 | −0.057 | — |","+","+Com-equ per asset, b = 0.2: negative in 21 of 24 asset-window cells (only NVDAX/test, SPCX/test and","+WTIOIL/val3 positive), and 22/24 at b = 0.1.","+","+Dev is three to four times better than the other two windows. The obvious explanation is staleness —","+dev starts five days after the fit, test two months after — so I rebuilt the artifact at 2026-07-23","+and 2026-08-25 and rescored each window against a level fitted immediately before it:","+","+| window | stale artifact | fresh artifact |","+|---|---:|---:|","+| dev | −0.171 | −0.171 |","+| val3 | −0.041 | −0.048 |","+| test | −0.037 | −0.048 |","+","+Freshness is worth 0.007 pp, not the missing 0.13. Dev is simply a kind window, and the honest","+out-of-sample expectation is the val3/test number. At the width that actually ships (`scale`","+{5: 0.90} with `SCALE_MAP`, 1000 paths, no level grid): **−0.168 / −0.026 / −0.039 %**, and the","+level optimum does not move — b = 0.2 is best at 0.90 on dev and test, and b = 0 already prefers","+0.92 on val3, so the blend carries no level correction of its own.","+","+**Verdict**: shipped for the eight com-equ assets at b = 0.2, `vlong_art=\"vlong_full.npz\"`. Crypto","+left at 0 — the 24-hour leg shows the same dev/val3-positive, test-negative flip that kept the","+vol-of-vol factor off, and the 1-hour leg is flat on val3. Scoping by asset also keeps the two","+crypto horizons consistent with each other, which a blend keyed on step size would not. Verified","+bit-identical on all twenty crypto prompts tested and changed on all sixteen com-equ ones, so the","+crypto-24h and crypto-1h official legs stand unmodified and only the eight com-equ legs were re-run.","+","+This is the first thing I have shipped whose out-of-sample size is *below* the 0.1 % bar the rest of","+the model is held to, and I want that on the record. It is shipped on the consistency of the sign,","+not the size: negative on three disjoint windows, at every b in 0.1–0.3, at four of five widths, in","+21 of 24 asset cells, and under two artifact vintages. Doubling the paths from 500 to 1000 moved the","+window means by 0.01–0.03 pp, so the measurement is window-limited, not Monte-Carlo-limited. The","+expected gain is about 0.04 % of one configuration — roughly 0.01 % of the score.","+","+**Lesson**: Iteration 16's redundancy principle said only information that is *not* already flowing","+through realized volatility can be incremental, and I read that as \"only forward-looking","+information.\" That was too narrow. This feature is entirely backward-looking; what makes it","+incremental is that it looks back *further than the context window reaches*. The served interface","+hands the model seven days, so anything about the asset on a longer timescale is outside it by","+construction and has to be carried in as an artifact. That is a second, separate source of","+non-redundant information, and it is the only one of the two I could actually act on — and its size,","+0.04 %, is a fair measure of how little is left on the table once the conditional level is right."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/workspace/agent/journal.md"]}}}
