{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYwQXvmVM5mH9pqqm9sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MqRDRo6egZSegZdgbFGLMo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 27 — The calendar's effect on width is convex, and one exponent cannot say so\n\n**Hypothesis**: suggestions.md item 12, finally tested. The model's only statement about how much of\nan asset's width follows the calendar is a single exponent on the time-of-week profile,\n`seas_gamma = 1.35` at the 5-minute step. A power is *linear in log-profile*. If the true relation\nbetween \"how dead is this bucket\" and \"how wide should the model be\" is not linear, no value of the\nexponent can express it, and the sweep that chose 1.35 was choosing the best straight line through a\ncurve.\n\n**Diagnostic first**. `agent/eda_profile.py` pools every 5-minute step of every path and reports\nmean|realized| / mean|simulated| by decile of the bent profile value. Two off-hour cadences, because\nof Iteration 20. Reproducible to three decimals between them:\n\n| profile decile | 0.34 | 0.53 | 0.69 | 0.83 | 0.98 | 1.17 | 1.47 | 2.09 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| com-equ ratio | 1.213 | 1.069 | 1.027 | 0.999 | 0.945 | 1.018 | 1.050 | 1.153 |\n| % exactly zero | 16.1 | 7.4 | 4.6 | 3.3 | 2.8 | 2.0 | 1.4 | 1.0 |\n\n| profile decile | 0.63 | 0.76 | 0.84 | 0.90 | 0.97 | 1.06 | 1.23 | 1.59 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| crypto ratio | 1.175 | 1.161 | 1.181 | 1.096 | 1.090 | 1.074 | 1.098 | 1.044 |\n\nCom-equ is **U-shaped**: relative to an average bucket the model is too narrow at *both* ends of the\ncalendar at once. That is convexity, and a power cannot produce it. Crypto is monotone decreasing —\nover-amplified, wanting a smaller exponent, which a power *can* produce.\n\nThe com-equ shape has a mechanism. The deadest decile has 16 % of its realized 5-minute returns\nexactly zero and still a 21 % *larger* mean absolute size than the ensemble. A closed session is not\na quiet diffusion; it is a point mass at zero plus occasional gap-sized prints. The CRPS-optimal\nwidth for that mixture is wider than the width that matches its bulk, so the buckets where the\nestimator sees the least action are exactly the ones where it under-serves.\n\n**Change**: `sv_model` has carried `seas_gamma_lo` — a second exponent applied below the weekly mean\n— since the activity experiment, and it had never been swept. `agent/exp_gamma_split.py` sweeps the\npair per asset class, with the width level re-optimised at every cell. Added `seas_gamma_map` and\n`seas_gamma_lo_map` so the two classes can differ at the 5-minute step without touching crypto-1h.\n\n**Result**. Com-equ, % vs the shipped single exponent, level re-optimised over 0.85–1.05:\n\n| g_hi \\ g_lo | 0.75 | 0.90 | 1.05 | 1.35 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1.35 | −0.10 / +0.11 / +0.46 | −0.11 / +0.02 / +0.28 | −0.11 / −0.01 / +0.16 | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| 1.65 | −0.20 / −0.09 / +0.10 | −0.19 / −0.12 / −0.02 | −0.14 / −0.13 / −0.11 | +0.03 / −0.04 / −0.19 |\n| 1.80 | −0.20 / −0.12 / −0.02 | **−0.16 / −0.14 / −0.12** | −0.10 / −0.11 / −0.19 | +0.12 / +0.01 / −0.23 |\n| 1.95 | −0.14 / −0.12 / −0.10 | −0.10 / −0.11 / −0.18 | −0.00 / −0.08 / −0.22 | +0.26 / +0.08 / −0.20 |\n\nA broad diagonal ridge, interior on both axes. Each window's own best cell differs, and test alone\nwould happily take `g_lo = 1.35` (no hinge, just a bigger exponent) — but that column is positive on\ndev at every g_hi, so the hinge is what all three agree on. (1.80, 0.90) is the point where they\nagree most evenly. At the shipped level with 1000 paths: **−0.178 / −0.058 / −0.126 %**, and the\nlevel optimum does not move enough to be worth a second knob (0.94 trades 0.04 pp of dev for 0.06 pp\nof val3).\n\n**Verdict**: shipped for the eight com-equ assets. Crypto rejected — and instructively. On a level\ngrid of (0.90, 0.95, 1.00) crypto's hinge measured −0.093 / −0.060 / −0.047, which would have\nshipped. Widening the grid to (0.85 … 1.05) let the *baseline* find a better level on test and the\ngain became −0.093 / −0.062 / **+0.004**. The entire crypto effect was a level improvement wearing a\nshape's clothes — Iteration 12's confound, caught only because the grid was widened for an unrelated\nreason.\n\n**Lesson**: two lessons, and the second is the one that nearly cost me. First: when a swept\nparameter sits at a clean interior optimum, that is evidence about the best value *within the\nfunctional form*, not evidence that the form is right. `seas_gamma = 1.35` had been swept four times\nacross this campaign and was correct every time; it was the best straight line through a curve, and\nthe diagnostic that found the curve took twenty minutes to write. Sweep harder is not the same as\nlook at the residual. Second: a level grid that does not bracket the optimum for *both* arms turns a\nlevel difference into a shape result. I have written \"re-optimise the level at every point\" in this\njournal since Iteration 12 and still got it wrong, because the grid was wide enough for the champion\nand not for the candidate. The rule needs the stronger form: the level grid has to be wide enough\nthat the optimum is interior *for every cell being compared*, and if any cell's optimum is at an\nedge the comparison is not yet a comparison.\nEOF\necho ok; grep -c ok /tmp/off_ce2.log 2>/dev/null","description":"Write the Iteration 27 journal entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":145387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"26fd5d1c-f5c4-4b8f-b701-3c8608c04494","timestamp":"2026-09-30T03:47:45.189Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MqRDRo6egZSegZdgbFGLMo","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"66e0b966-a844-4f6a-b2fd-b8e848c7a04f","timestamp":"2026-09-30T03:47:45.260Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\n0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"returnCodeInterpretation":"No matches found","noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/journal.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1181,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1181,"newLines":75,"lines":[" marginal, and between nu = 3 and nu = 6 the bulk of a standardised Student-t barely moves — so a"," correctly measured, genuinely asset-specific, genuinely non-redundant quantity produced exactly zero"," CRPS, for the third time in this campaign. Measure the sensitivity before fitting the parameter.","+","+## Iteration 27 — The calendar's effect on width is convex, and one exponent cannot say so","+","+**Hypothesis**: suggestions.md item 12, finally tested. The model's only statement about how much of","+an asset's width follows the calendar is a single exponent on the time-of-week profile,","+`seas_gamma = 1.35` at the 5-minute step. A power is *linear in log-profile*. If the true relation","+between \"how dead is this bucket\" and \"how wide should the model be\" is not linear, no value of the","+exponent can express it, and the sweep that chose 1.35 was choosing the best straight line through a","+curve.","+","+**Diagnostic first**. `agent/eda_profile.py` pools every 5-minute step of every path and reports","+mean|realized| / mean|simulated| by decile of the bent profile value. Two off-hour cadences, because","+of Iteration 20. Reproducible to three decimals between them:","+","+| profile decile | 0.34 | 0.53 | 0.69 | 0.83 | 0.98 | 1.17 | 1.47 | 2.09 |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| com-equ ratio | 1.213 | 1.069 | 1.027 | 0.999 | 0.945 | 1.018 | 1.050 | 1.153 |","+| % exactly zero | 16.1 | 7.4 | 4.6 | 3.3 | 2.8 | 2.0 | 1.4 | 1.0 |","+","+| profile decile | 0.63 | 0.76 | 0.84 | 0.90 | 0.97 | 1.06 | 1.23 | 1.59 |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| crypto ratio | 1.175 | 1.161 | 1.181 | 1.096 | 1.090 | 1.074 | 1.098 | 1.044 |","+","+Com-equ is **U-shaped**: relative to an average bucket the model is too narrow at *both* ends of the","+calendar at once. That is convexity, and a power cannot produce it. Crypto is monotone decreasing —","+over-amplified, wanting a smaller exponent, which a power *can* produce.","+","+The com-equ shape has a mechanism. The deadest decile has 16 % of its realized 5-minute returns","+exactly zero and still a 21 % *larger* mean absolute size than the ensemble. A closed session is not","+a quiet diffusion; it is a point mass at zero plus occasional gap-sized prints. The CRPS-optimal","+width for that mixture is wider than the width that matches its bulk, so the buckets where the","+estimator sees the least action are exactly the ones where it under-serves.","+","+**Change**: `sv_model` has carried `seas_gamma_lo` — a second exponent applied below the weekly mean","+— since the activity experiment, and it had never been swept. `agent/exp_gamma_split.py` sweeps the","+pair per asset class, with the width level re-optimised at every cell. Added `seas_gamma_map` and","+`seas_gamma_lo_map` so the two classes can differ at the 5-minute step without touching crypto-1h.","+","+**Result**. Com-equ, % vs the shipped single exponent, level re-optimised over 0.85–1.05:","+","+| g_hi \\ g_lo | 0.75 | 0.90 | 1.05 | 1.35 |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| 1.35 | −0.10 / +0.11 / +0.46 | −0.11 / +0.02 / +0.28 | −0.11 / −0.01 / +0.16 | 0 / 0 / 0 |","+| 1.65 | −0.20 / −0.09 / +0.10 | −0.19 / −0.12 / −0.02 | −0.14 / −0.13 / −0.11 | +0.03 / −0.04 / −0.19 |","+| 1.80 | −0.20 / −0.12 / −0.02 | **−0.16 / −0.14 / −0.12** | −0.10 / −0.11 / −0.19 | +0.12 / +0.01 / −0.23 |","+| 1.95 | −0.14 / −0.12 / −0.10 | −0.10 / −0.11 / −0.18 | −0.00 / −0.08 / −0.22 | +0.26 / +0.08 / −0.20 |","+","+A broad diagonal ridge, interior on both axes. Each window's own best cell differs, and test alone","+would happily take `g_lo = 1.35` (no hinge, just a bigger exponent) — but that column is positive on","+dev at every g_hi, so the hinge is what all three agree on. (1.80, 0.90) is the point where they","+agree most evenly. At the shipped level with 1000 paths: **−0.178 / −0.058 / −0.126 %**, and the","+level optimum does not move enough to be worth a second knob (0.94 trades 0.04 pp of dev for 0.06 pp","+of val3).","+","+**Verdict**: shipped for the eight com-equ assets. Crypto rejected — and instructively. On a level","+grid of (0.90, 0.95, 1.00) crypto's hinge measured −0.093 / −0.060 / −0.047, which would have","+shipped. Widening the grid to (0.85 … 1.05) let the *baseline* find a better level on test and the","+gain became −0.093 / −0.062 / **+0.004**. The entire crypto effect was a level improvement wearing a","+shape's clothes — Iteration 12's confound, caught only because the grid was widened for an unrelated","+reason.","+","+**Lesson**: two lessons, and the second is the one that nearly cost me. First: when a swept","+parameter sits at a clean interior optimum, that is evidence about the best value *within the","+functional form*, not evidence that the form is right. `seas_gamma = 1.35` had been swept four times","+across this campaign and was correct every time; it was the best straight line through a curve, and","+the diagnostic that found the curve took twenty minutes to write. Sweep harder is not the same as","+look at the residual. Second: a level grid that does not bracket the optimum for *both* arms turns a","+level difference into a shape result. I have written \"re-optimise the level at every point\" in this","+journal since Iteration 12 and still got it wrong, because the grid was wide enough for the champion","+and not for the candidate. The rule needs the stronger form: the level grid has to be wide enough","+that the optimum is interior *for every cell being compared*, and if any cell's optimum is at an","+edge the comparison is not yet a comparison."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/workspace/agent/journal.md"]}}}
