{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfYyZCtnBMBvpfmyzxVoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XGspsFCjEvkSLkoJWUartn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess\nnew = subprocess.run([\"uv\",\"run\",\"python\",\"agent/results_table.py\",\"off_champ4.json\",\"off_base.json\"],\n                     capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\nblk = new.split(\"**COM_EQU_24H**\")[1].split(\"**CRYPTO_1H**\")[0]\np=\"agent/report.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"**COM_EQU_24H**\"); j=s.index(\"**CRYPTO_1H**\", i)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s[:i]+\"**COM_EQU_24H**\"+blk+s[j:]); print(\"ok\")\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n**Official re-run.** Again only the eight com-equ legs changed. COM_EQU_24H 1820.7 → **1817.9**\nagainst 2076.5 — **−12.32 % to −12.45 %**. The hinge is the largest single gain since the seasonal\nexponent itself.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'MSG'\nThe calendar's effect on width is convex; one exponent could only fit a straight line\n\neda_profile.py stratifies the dispersion ratio by time-of-week profile value and finds\nthe com-equ relation is U-shaped: relative to an average bucket the model is too narrow\nat BOTH ends of the calendar. A power is linear in log-profile and cannot express that.\nThe deadest decile has 16 % of its realized 5-minute returns exactly zero and still a\n21 % larger mean absolute size than the ensemble -- a closed session is a point mass plus\ngap-sized jumps, and the CRPS-optimal width for that mixture is wider than its bulk.\n\nsv_model has carried an unswept `seas_gamma_lo` (a second exponent below the weekly mean)\nsince the activity experiment. Swept jointly per asset class it gives a broad interior\nridge; (1.80, 0.90) is where all three windows agree, worth -0.178 / -0.058 / -0.126 % at\nthe shipped level. Official COM_EQU_24H 1820.7 -> 1817.9 (-12.32 % -> -12.45 %); crypto\nlegs bit-identical. Added seas_gamma_map / seas_gamma_lo_map so the classes can differ at\nthe 5-minute step without touching crypto-1h.\n\nCrypto rejected, instructively: on a (0.90, 0.95, 1.00) level grid its hinge measured\n-0.093 / -0.060 / -0.047 and would have shipped. Widening the grid let the BASELINE find\na better level on test and the gain became -0.093 / -0.062 / +0.004. Iteration 12's level\nconfound, caught only because the grid was widened for an unrelated reason. The rule needs\nits stronger form: the level grid must bracket the optimum for every cell being compared.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\n)\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Patch the results table and commit iteration 27"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1752,"cache_read_input_tokens":152120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1752,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"89b63657-d5d0-4aa9-ba68-b1638cfb94a4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T04:15:42.003Z"}
