{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single genuine user message in the entire campaign was: **\"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"** (plus a continuation instruction to resume from a prior summary without recapping, and the final instruction to produce this summary as text only).\n\n   `/workspace/agent/CAMPAIGN.md` is the campaign constitution:\n   - **Objective**: build the price-simulation model with the lowest **CRPS** (lower = better) for Synth Bittensor subnet SN50, across three scoring configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC/ETH/SOL/XRP/HYPE, 86400s/300s, 289 pts), COM_EQU_24H (XAU/NVDAX/GOOGLX/TSLAX/AAPLX/WTIOIL/SPCX/SP500, 86400s/300s), CRYPTO_1H (crypto, 3600s/60s, 61 pts). 1000 simulations per prompt; honour whatever `num_simulations` is passed.\n   - **Judge every experiment on CRPS**, per configuration and per asset. \"Never trade a CRPS regression for a better one.\"\n   - Champion is evaluated over the **10 days following the 2026-09-14 data cutoff**.\n   - Work solo; no one can answer questions; record decisions in the journal.\n   - **Envelope**: 100.00 USD credits, 18h wall-clock. Read `agent/BUDGET.md` **at the start of each iteration**; a LANDING ORDER there is non-negotiable.\n   - **\"Nominating is final** — the first time you stop while `agent/CHAMPION` exists, your campaign is over: you will not be resumed, and every remaining dollar and hour is forfeited. Until then you may keep iterating and amend your nomination. Nominate early only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score. **A champion is MANDATORY.** What is scored is how strong your champion is, not whether you dared to nominate one: ending with no `agent/CHAMPION` is a Score of 0 and a wasted leg — strictly worse than nominating something imperfect.\"\n   - **Hardware**: GCP g2-standard-16, 14 CPU / 48GB RAM / 1× NVIDIA L4; only one GPU job at a time.\n\n   **Constraints stated verbatim in CAMPAIGN.md that MUST continue to apply:**\n   1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat everything after **2026-09-14** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and invalidates the result. Audited on your transcript.\n   2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges, aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n   3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester` (via `agent/predict.py`). One implementation of the metric is what makes results comparable. NEVER reimplement the metric.\n   4. Not allowed: falsifying the journal or results; reproducing another participant's served output as your own.\n   5. **Keep binary and encoded data out of your terminal output.** Read parquet with pandas and `.npy` with numpy — never `cat` a parquet, a git bundle, or model weights, and never pipe base64 into your context.\n   6. **Start from public sources only**: synth-lib, synth-subnet, the Synth API, and your own ideas. The operator's existing miner models are not part of your materials and must not inform your work; if any turns up, leave it unread and note it in `suggestions.md`.\n   7. Final champion must expose in `agent/modeling.py`: `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` -> `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`, each path `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context. `context_prices` is a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days preceding `start_time` with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`; it MAY CONTAIN NaN — **drop, never interpolate**. Must run OFFLINE.\n   8. **If the model uses randomness, seed it from `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED`** — read once at the top of `simulate()`, seed every generator; fall back to a chosen seed when absent.\n   - Operational rules: always run commands from the workspace root; `market_data/` is READ-ONLY; run everything through `uv run`; don't backtest across the three structural breaks (2026-06-23 competition split, 2026-03-11 crypto-1h formula change, ~2026-07-17 SPYX retired / SP500 introduced — **SPYX is DEAD**).\n\n   **Required deliverables (in `agent/`, in English, committed to git):** `journal.md` (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson per iteration), `report.md` (explainer style for Synth miners), `CHAMPION` (YAML: `sha` = an EXISTING git commit, `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles` `[low, high]`, `notes` MUST include backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths from `agent/predict.py` alongside the starting-point CRPS; \"The harness checks the interface as soon as this file appears (result in BUDGET.md) — fix it if the check fails\"), `suggestions.md`.\n\n   **Mid-conversation system instruction (still in effect):** while bypass permissions mode is active, do work through the Bash tool wherever it can accomplish the job (cat/sed/grep/heredocs/short scripts) rather than the dedicated Read/Edit/Write tools; fall back to a dedicated tool only when Bash genuinely cannot do the job.\n\n   **Git attribution reminder (still in effect):** end git commit messages with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`; end PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **CRPS decomposition**: validator score = sum of **univariate** CRPS terms on relative price changes over intervals, in bps. No multivariate term. 24h: 5min 288 terms ≈61%, 30min 48 ≈25%, 3hour 8 ≈10%, 24hour_abs 1 ≈3.6%. CRYPTO_1H adds a `*_gaps` block (~29%) plus `vol_scoring_blocks`; the 24h competitions have empty `vol_scoring_blocks`.\n   - **The central identity**: `E CRPS(σ) = sqrt(2/π)·sqrt(1+σ²) − σ/sqrt(π)`, minimised at σ=1; `E CRPS(σ)/E CRPS(1) ≈ 1 + 0.25·(log σ)²`. A constant scale error is nearly free; the entire recoverable CRPS is `Var(log σ̂ − log σ_true)`.\n   - **The oracle gap**: ≈6% better than the causal champion on crypto-24h.\n   - **The level confound (Iter 12, strengthened in Iter 27)**: sweep shape parameters with the level re-optimised at every point — **and the level grid must bracket the optimum for EVERY cell being compared, including the baseline. If any cell's argmin sits at a grid edge, the comparison is not yet a comparison.**\n   - **The transfer criterion**: parameter stability under refitting predicts out-of-sample transfer better than in-sample gain. Effects under ~0.1%, or disagreeing in sign between windows, are noise. **Sign consistency across disjoint windows/assets/parameter values is separate evidence from magnitude** (Iter 25 shipped on sign; Iter 26 rejected on lack of sign).\n   - **The redundancy principle (Iter 16, corrected in Iter 25)**: a feature is incremental iff it is outside the span of what a fast EWMA of the 7-day context can see — which can be because it is in the future, **or because it is further in the past than the context window extends**.\n   - **The sensitivity boundary (Iter 26)**: long-horizon information only pays where the score is sensitive; the score is sensitive to *width* and almost nothing else.\n   - **Convexity of the calendar dependence (Iter 27-28)**: a power of the time-of-week profile is linear in log-profile; the true relation is convex (com-equ U-shaped) so a hinge at the weekly mean is needed. Quiet buckets are under-served at both horizons.\n   - **The round-hour prompt-grid artifact (Iter 20)**: a cadence dividing an hour always lands on :00; use 173/97 minutes for absolute calibration diagnostics.\n   - Three validation windows: **dev** 2026-07-05..07-23, **val3** 2026-07-24..08-25, **test** 2026-08-26..09-13 (1h test ends 09-12).\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/BUDGET.md`** (harness-maintained, read-only). Last read: `Credits: 83.64 / 100.00 USD (84%)`, `Time: 12.1 h elapsed, 5.9 h remaining (67%)`, `Phase: normal`. **Must be re-read at the start of each iteration.**\n\n   - **`/workspace/agent/modeling.py`** — champion entry point. Current state after this session's three ships:\n     ```python\n     VOV_MAP = {a: 0.30 for a in SCALE_MAP}\n\n     # Shrink each asset's reversion target toward a long-run level fitted offline over the whole\n     # snapshot (agent/vlong.py). ... Worth -0.17 / -0.03 / -0.04 % ... journal Iteration 25.\n     LONG_BLEND_MAP = {a: 0.20 for a in SCALE_MAP}\n\n     # Exponent on the time-of-week profile, keyed by step size in minutes. ...\n     SEAS_GAMMA = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.85}\n\n     # Two exponents instead of one, hinged at the weekly mean, for the eight session-traded assets.\n     # ... journal Iteration 27.\n     SEAS_GAMMA_MAP = {a: {5: 1.80} for a in SCALE_MAP}\n     SEAS_GAMMA_LO_MAP = {a: {5: 0.90} for a in SCALE_MAP}\n\n     # The same correction at the 1-minute step, where it needs no asset map: only crypto has a\n     # 1-hour competition ... The high side keeps its shipped 0.85.\n     SEAS_GAMMA_LO = {5: 1.35, 1: 0.40}\n\n     CHAMPION_SPEC = (\n         \"sv_model\",\n         {\n             \"profile\": \"tow_full.npz\",\n             \"seasonal\": True,\n             \"seas_gamma\": SEAS_GAMMA,\n             \"scale\": SCALE,                    # {5: 0.90, 1: 0.95}\n             \"scale_map\": SCALE_MAP,\n             \"vov_map\": VOV_MAP,\n             \"vov_halflife\": 144.0,\n             \"vlong_art\": \"vlong_full.npz\",\n             \"long_blend_map\": LONG_BLEND_MAP,\n             \"seas_gamma_lo\": SEAS_GAMMA_LO,\n             \"seas_gam