{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfZ35TtbfonraEVGy6Un7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VdMoQyU49rd3Z4sfHNNeEv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"agent/report.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"* **The seasonality artifact is fitted on the whole snapshot**, so the backtested numbers in §6\n  are mildly optimistic relative to a truly causal run. The validation numbers quoted throughout\n  §4–§5 all use artifacts fitted strictly before their window, and the effects survive there.\n\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"* **The three committed artifacts are fitted on the whole snapshot** — the time-of-week profiles\n  (`tow_full.npz`), the long-run volatility levels (`vlong_full.npz`) and the per-asset exponent\n  maps — so the backtested numbers in §6 are mildly optimistic relative to a truly causal run.\n  The validation numbers quoted throughout §4–§5 all use artifacts fitted strictly before their\n  window, and the effects survive there. For the evaluation window this cuts the other way: the\n  artifacts are 10 to 24 days stale by the end of it. The long-run levels were tested for exactly\n  this (refit at three cutoffs, §4) and move by less than the effect they carry; the profiles are\n  a calendar and do not go stale on that timescale.\n* **The two residual mis-calibrations I know about are priced, not fixed.** After the two-sided\n  exponent, com-equ is ~4 % too narrow near the weekly mean and crypto-24h runs a monotone width\n  gradient across the profile. Both are real and reproduce at two prompt cadences. Neither is\n  worth fitting: §2's identity bounds them at 0.02 % and 0.06 % of CRPS respectively, and a direct\n  CRPS test of the crypto one returned +0.004 %.\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\nPY\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'MSG'\nClose the two open residuals in the documents, with numbers rather than intentions\n\nThe report's limitations now state what is still mis-calibrated and what it is worth:\n0.02 % for the com-equ hump about the hinge, 0.06 % for the crypto-24h width gradient,\nagainst a measured +0.004 % when the second was tested directly. Also generalises the\nin-sample-artifact caveat from the profiles to all three committed artifacts, and notes\nthat staleness over the evaluation window was tested for the one artifact that can go\nstale.\n\nsuggestions.md gains the three items the campaign earned the right to write: do not fit\nthe quadratic bend, price a residual in CRPS units before chasing it, and count cells\nrather than basis points.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\n)\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Finalise report limitations and commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1296,"cache_read_input_tokens":61616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1296,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fdc998-0d4c-4bec-aa01-713aae481473","uuid":"d7e78ae8-019a-44f7-a7bd-c6001090774d","timestamp":"2026-09-30T05:01:56.959Z"}
